\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen on backfoot as returning confidence dulls safe-haven allure\b0\par\par\uc2 653 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 August 2019\par 02:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Graphic: World \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates in 2019 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://tmsnrt.rs/2egbfVh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://tmsnrt.rs/2egbfVh}}}\par \par \uc2 * Temporary calm descends on \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market\par \par \uc2 * Stock gains overnight ease risk aversion\par \par \uc2 * Markets still on edge over trade war, Brexit\par \par \uc2 By Stanley White\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Aug 29 (Reuters) - The dollar held gains against the safe-haven yen on Thursday as ebbing recession worries soothed markets after earlier volatility although the pound nursed its losses as investors became increasingly worried about a hard Brexit.\par \par \uc2 Sterling fell 0.6% against the greenback on Wednesday after British Prime Minister \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  moved to suspend parliament, seen as a bid to limit debate ahead of the Oct. 31 deadline for the UK to leave the \uc2 European Union\uc2 . That increased expectations of a "no-deal Brexit," which would mean a departure without trading agreements in place.\par \par \uc2 In Asian trade, investors will keep a close eye on stock markets, following gains on Wall Street overnight, as well as the \uc2 Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's daily yuan fixing and any news of U.S.-China trade talks.\par \par \uc2 Sentiment in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is likely to remain fragile, because there are still signs of stress. The \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yield curve remains inverted, which is commonly considered a sign of an impending recession.\par \par \uc2 "The gains in stocks have provided some temporary relief to risk sentiment, which has allowed the dollar to reclaim the 106 yen mark," said Minori Uchida, head of global markets research at \uc2 MUFG Bank\uc2  in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 "This is likely temporary, because we are still very much worried about tariffs. In addition, long-term yields show that Fed is behind the curve on rate cuts."\par \par \uc2 Yields on 30-year Treasuries have hit a record low as investors scramble for the safety of government debt.\par \par \uc2 Against the dollar, the yen was steady early in Asian trading at 106.06 yen after falling 0.3% on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index, which measures the greenback against a basket of six major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rose 0.16% to 98.189.\par \par \uc2 Spot gold was flat at $1,539.65 per ounce, following a 0.2% decline on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The yen and gold are both considered safe-haven assets, so they tend to weaken when other financial markets show signs that risk aversion has abated.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed little reaction after U.S. Treasury Secretary \uc2 Steven Mnuchin\uc2  said he has no intention of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the dollar right now, according to Bloomberg.\par \par \uc2 However, traders may remain concerned about U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy because President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has complained that the dollar is too strong and has repeatedly attacked the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  for not cutting interest rates further.\par \par \uc2 Many traders say such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely, especially after the United States labelled \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 Still, there is some concern given Trump's often erratic statements about the Fed and about negotiations with China to solve the trade war.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration on Wednesday made official its extra 5% tariff on $300 billion in Chinese imports and set collection dates of Sept. 1 and Dec. 15, prompting hundreds of U.S. retail, footwear, toy and technology companies to warn of price hikes.\par \par \uc2 The trade dispute between the United States and China is now in its second year and is placing increasing strain on the global economy, forcing policy makers to respond with interest rate cuts and stimulus measures to bolster growth.\par \par \uc2 The pound held steady at $1.2217 on Thursday and was last quoted at 90.74 pence per euro, following a 0.5% decline on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The suspension of UK parliament, which had to be approved by Queen Elizabeth, limits the time opponents have to derail a disorderly Brexit, but also increases the chance that Johnson could face a vote of no-confidence in his government, and possibly an election. (Reporting by Stanley White; Editing by Sam Holmes) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-8-29T01:39:26.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190829ef8t001b9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
