\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 IMF\uc2 : \uc2 Chinese  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  has  \highlight22\uc2 intervened \highlight\uc2  little on yearly change in recent years\b0\par\par\uc2 436 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 DREAMSTIMEEXPANSIONThe International Monetary Fund (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ) today assured that the \uc2 People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 PBOC\uc2 , central) has had "few \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 " on the yuan's exchange rate against foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent years.\par \par \uc2 In a report published today on the Chinese economy in the past year, the agency cites as an example that after the devaluation of the renminbi (official name of the yuan) recorded between June and August 2018, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained "generally stable" compared to the main international \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This report is published the same week in which the yuan first crossed the psychological barrier of 7 units per dollar since 2008; some analysts believe that the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  deliberately allowed this drop in response to US President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's announcement that it would impose new tariffs of 10% to $300 billion of Chinese imports.\par \par \uc2 The yuan's loss of value didn't sit well in the United States, and that country's Treasury Department officially designated China as a "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator" country, something Trump had been insisting on for years.\par \par \uc2 This movement assumes, under U.S. law, that Washington and Beijing must now negotiate directly or through the \uc2 IMF\uc2  to address alleged irregularities in Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange rates.\par \par \uc2 However, both the authorities and the official Chinese press have shown outrage at the accusation, so it seems highly unlikely that Beijing will lend itself to negotiate on the issue.\par \par \uc2 And while the \uc2 IMF\uc2  report covers until July 31 this year, its conclusions are that the effective real exchange rate complies with the basic rules.\par \par \uc2 However, the document emphasizes that China should be more transparent in explaining the movements of the yuan and that the authorities should allow greater flexibility in their exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 Currently, the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  sets a benchmark rate every day (yesterday's, for example, it was 7,0136 yuan for every dollar) and allows the onshore rate - the one quoted in local markets - to fluctuate a maximum of 2%.\par \par \uc2 However, the reference rate for international investors, the offshore, is listed on foreign markets such as Hong Kong and is not regulated by the \uc2 PBOC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The official press soon echoed the news: State agency \uc2 Xinhua\uc2  today quoted Columbia University economics professor \uc2 Jeffrey Sachs\uc2 , who believes that "the \uc2 IMF\uc2  report makes clear that there has been no \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation" in China.\par \par \uc2 On Washington and Beijing's long-running trade war since March 2018 and overcriss in recent weeks, the \uc2 IMF\uc2  recognizes the economic "great uncertainty" in the short term, and advises China, if the situation worsens, to pull stimulus mainly tax prosecutors.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020190810ef8a00317\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
