me soon, even as the U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade war risks morphing into a global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war. Any such overt action, even to smooth volatile market flows, could be construed as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation by the Trump administration. Despite the amicable relationship between U.S. President Trump and Japan's PM Abe, the U.S. is fast approaching a key election year and the current administration will likely continue to take a "no holds barred" approach to international relations. A caution flag would probably go up should USD/JPY fall below 100 but, in the absence of such a development, the MOF will likely stick to verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This does not mean the Japanese government will not urge pension funds and semi-official entities to prop up USD/JPY at key levels. To wit, such activity has been talked about in the Tokyo markets and widely reported in the press. Such moves do not really pose an inconvenience for many of these entities who are hungry for positive yield.\par \par \uc2 To read our latest \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  news and analysis services, click on\par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-8-11T04:27:28.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190808ef8800id5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
