\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Opening of markets: scholarships and interest recovery. Oil gains more than 2% with Saudi Arabia  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 773 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 August 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Green is now the dominant color in the scholarship markets, after \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  has come back to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and alleviate the fears of investors. The bags go up and the interest recovers. Oil is firing more than 2% after Saudi Arabia has made it clear that it will do whatever it takes to keep the raw material prices from sinking. The markets in Numbers\par \par \uc2 PSI-20 values 0.88% for 4,879.85 points\par \par \uc2 Stoxx 600 wins 0.81% for 371.6 points\par \par \uc2 Nikkei valued 0.37% to 20,593.35 points\par \par \uc2 Interest of the Portuguese debt to ten years rises 3.5 basis points to 0.213%\par \par \uc2 Euro enjoys 0.18%% to 1.1219 dollars\par \par \uc2 Oil in London rises 2.21% to 57.47 dollars a barrel\par \par \par \par \uc2 Europe recovers for the second consecutive session\par \par \uc2 In Europe, the start of the session is positive with the Stoxx 600, the index that aggregates the 600 main European quoted, to value 0.81% for the 371.6 points. Despite the appreciation for the second consecutive session, the Stoxx 600 still failed to recover from the strong losses of last week.\par \par \par \par \uc2 The European scholarship market is today infected by the Green wave of Asia where the scholarships valued. To give investors optimism was the exchange rate set by the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2 , which contributed to the appreciation of the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar, removing the worries that marked the start of the week and provoked strong falls in the four corners of World.\par \par \par \par \uc2 The valuations are transversal to almost all sectors of the Stoxx 600, with special emphasis on the technological and health sector. Among the quoted, there is good and bad news. \uc2 Deutsche Telekom\uc2  saw its profits increase 7.1% while Thyssenkrupp presented a quarterly loss of 94 million euros, having made another profit warning.\par \par \par \par \uc2 In the main European squares, the investor sentiment is also positive. This is the case of the PSI-20 that is valuing 0.88% for 4,879.85 points, also accumulating two sessions in high. In the ascents the highlight goes to the BCP, which interrupts a cycle of 11 falls, for \uc2 EDP Renov\u225\'00\'E1veis\uc2 , which reached historical maxima, and for \uc2 Galp Energia\uc2  that rises on a day when the oil recovers between 2 to 3%.\par \par \par \par \uc2 Interest rises and relients maximum\par \par \uc2 The interest rates associated with sovereign debt are rising at all times and in the majority of countries, on a day when investors seem to be relieving pressure on markets.\par \par \par \par \uc2 Thus, the implicit rate in the 10-year debt of Portugal is rising 3.5 basis points to 0.213%. The German rate is advancing 2 points to 0.565%.\par \par \par \par \uc2 Yuan rises after new \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is valuing against the dollar, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has fixed an exchange rate (from which the renminbi may vary below or above) "stronger" than expected by analysts. The people's Bank of China gives some security to investors who want the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stabilised against the dollar.\u160\'00\'A0The yuan is rising 0.3% to 7.0039 yuan per dollar.\par \par \par \par \uc2 Oil rises more than 2% with Saudi Arabia \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Saudi Arabia is committed to not letting oil prices sink and, after the steep declines observed in recent days \u8211\'20\'13 that have led Brent to glide more than 20% since April-, contacted other oil producers to discuss potential Responses from theSector.\u160\'00\'A0\par \par \uc2 Saudi Arabia will not tolerate a continuous decline in oil prices \u8211\'20\'13 which have declined to seven months minimum \u8211\'20\'13 and is considering all the hypotheses, reveals Bloomberg, who cites the official source of Saudi Arabia.\par \par \par \par \uc2 Oil prices have experienced heavy declines in recent days, greatly due to fears related to a contraction of the world economy, in an environment of high uncertainty over the U.S.-China trade war. Contributing to the descent of the last session \u8211\'20\'13 which dragged prices to seven months minimum \u8211\'20\'13 was also the increase in U.S. reserves.\par \par \uc2 The price of the barrel of Brent, negotiated in London and reference to Portugal, is rising 2.21% to 57.47 dollars.\par \par \par \par \uc2 Nickel shoots for maximum April 2018\par \par \uc2 Nickel fired 13% to 16,690 dollars a tonne at a time when it speculated that Indonesia is restricting its export policy of this metal.\par \par \par \par \uc2 The gold is receding 0.24% to 1,497.57 dollars per ounce, after yesterday having surpassed, for the first time, the 1,500 dollars, with investors taking refuge in this precious metal due to fears surrounding the trade war and its economic impacts.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020190808ef88002h5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
