\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 China warns of chaos in the world over tariff war with US\b0\par\par\uc2 409 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Washington's decision to label the Beijing government a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator "will severely damage the international economic order and cause a chaos in financial markets," \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Added to this was the \uc2 People's Bank of China (PBOC) \uc2 which stated that the Us announcement will avoid a recovery in trade and the economy, since it ensured that China will not use exchange rates as a tool to deal with disputes Commercial.\par \par \uc2 In the past few days, the United States accused China of manipulating the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange situation, further opening the gap between the two economic powers and driving away any hope from a short-term resolution of the trade dispute.\par \par \uc2 China's alleged manipulation of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gives the United States more legal arguments to continue taking action against the Asian nation beyond tariffs.\par \par \uc2 It should be noted that the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ) disclosed three weeks ago that the value of the yuan was in line with China's economic fundamentals, while the dollar is overvalued at between 6% and 12%.\par \par \uc2 U.S. law sets three criteria for identifying manipulation between its trading partners: a global current account surplus, a significant trade surplus with the United States, and persistent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the exchange markets , notes Expansion.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's media warned that Beijing could use its dominant position as a rare earth exporter to the United States to press the trade dispute.\par \par \uc2 Fiscal stimulus\par \par \uc2 China announced that it will launch a special fiscal policy in the Shanghai Free Trade Area to promote free trade as the protracted trade dispute in Beijing and Washington threatens to lead to a total economic war.\par \par \uc2 In addition, it will grant crude oil import licences to qualified companies and implement preferential tax policies to firms operating in the fields of artificial intelligence, civil aviation, semiconductors and biopharmaceuticals.\par \par \uc2 In addition to the above, Shanghai Deputy Mayor Chen Yin added that foreign firms may not be subject to levies on transiting goods are stored in the area.\par \par \uc2 It should be noted that US President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  loathed China by threatening last week with 10% tariffs on U.S. imports worth $300 billion as of September 1.\par \par \uc2 However, analysts have warned that retaliatory measures as part of this commercial war could seriously damage the growth prospects, affecting investor confidence and the global landscape.\par \par \uc2 With information from Expansion.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020190807ef8600135\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
