\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Latin America's  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  recovered after china's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  measures\b0\par\par\uc2 375 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Latin American coins recovered Tuesday from the heavy losses of the previous session or moderated theirfalls, after \b \highlight22\uc2 China intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the dropping of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had broken in the previous session the psychological barrier of seven units per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The trade war between the world's two largest economies is on going on, but the tension seemed to moderate when the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2  (central) set a stronger middle ground in the yuan's contribution range, helping to calm the nerves of the Investors.\par \par \uc2 "The signal that China is somewhat unwilling to continue allowing a yen to fall beyond seven units per dollar is constructive from the cross-cutting perspective of assets," said Bipan Rai, an exchange rate strategy analyst at CIBC Capital Markets in Toronto.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso quoted with a slight loss of 0.05%. Meanwhile, the S&P/BMV IPC index benchmark was up 0.57% driven mainly by opportunity purchases.\par \par \uc2 The Colombian peso recovered by 0.87% after the sharp collapse of the previous session that took it to its lowest level in history. The COLCAP index of the stock exchange rose by 0.65%, with agents turning their attention to the publication of financial results for the second quarter of the companies.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso rose 0.94% favored by an improvement in global markets and after closing in the previous day at a minimum of more than three and a half years. Meanwhile, the main index of the Santiago Stock Exchange, IPSA, yielded just 0.05%.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real appreciated by 0.55% and the Bovespa stock index advanced by 2.06%.\par \par \uc2 In Peru, the sun was strengthened by 0.34% after six days of considerable losses, although local banks operated with short positions so traders are waiting for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . For its part, the benchmark of the Limean stock market dropped by a marginal 0.01%.\par \par \uc2 The Argentine peso appreciated by 0.45%, while the S&P Merval stock index won 1.08%. Operators added that the external factor adds the natural prudence generated by the closeness of the primary elections to be held this Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020190807ef860012n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
