\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 China drops yuan to lowsince 2008 in response to new US tariff barrier\b0\par\par\uc2 788 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 A new chapter in the trade war was written yesterday. China in retaliation to US President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's new decision to impose additional 10% tariffs on Chinese imports worth US$300 billion from September 1, responded with an ace up his sleeve, and one that knows annoying to the representative: the yuan.\par \par \uc2 His strategy aimed to let his \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fall to 7 yuan for every dollar. The 1.4% crash occurred yesterday and set a record number in the values recorded more than a decade ago.\par \par \uc2 This measure had immediate effects on the rest of the world, as the main exchanges began and ended the day in red.\par \par \uc2 In Chile was no exception: the dollar rose $7.5 compared to Friday to close at $720.80 its highest level since January 25, 2016. In turn, copper fell 2.11% to $2.56.\par \par \uc2 The reasonsAnalysts estimate that the \uc2 People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  has consciously dropped the value of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , without \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb it as in previous occasions.\par \par \uc2 Through a statement issued by the \uc2 People's Bank of China (PBOC) \uc2 on its website, Governor \uc2 Yi Gang\uc2  rejected the nation's use of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a tool to deal with external turbulence such as trade warfare, and anticipated that no would involve competitive devaluation. "The \uc2 PBOC\uc2  has the experience, confidence and capacity to keep the yuan's exchange rate basically stable at a reasonable and balanced level," the official statement said.\par \par \uc2 How does it affect you?A weaker yuan means that a substantial amount of goods and services exported by China are cheaper and can be further reduced, increasing the competitiveness of manufactured goods in its factories.\par \par \uc2 One of the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2 's main complaints in the context of the trade dispute, even before, is the allegation that Beijing allegedly manipulates its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent it from appreciating too much and therefore losing its exports Competitiveness. I mean, I'd keep it artificially low.\par \par \uc2 The fact that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has linked the depreciation to the tariffs shows that they have "turned the exchange rate" into a weapon, according to Julian Evans-Pritchard, an analyst at the consultancy \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2 . "They have almost given up hopes for a trade agreement with the United States," he adds.\par \par \uc2 "China slumped the price of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to an almost historic low. That's called 'exchange rate manipulation'. Are you listening to the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 ? It's a big breach that will weaken China a lot over time!" tweeted Trump. The US later officially declared China a manipulative country of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In addition, the \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2  government called on state-owned enterprises to suspend imports of U.S. agricultural products, bloomberg-related sources confirmed. This disruption could further increase tensions with Trump, who accuses the Asian giant of unfairly managing its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and not delivering on promises to buy more American crops.\par \par \uc2 Rosario National University's economist Julio Gambina said Beijing's response "is a game in the context of the negotiations taking over between the US and China" and noted that the measure "complicates the world economy." Gambina anticipates that U.S. businesses and consumers will be the "major injured," considering that China has greater social lysed defense mechanisms and the current economic policy plan, as opposed to the situation of his American adversary.\par \par \uc2 Louis Kujis, head of Oxford Economics for Asia, believes that "further weakeningyuan, could be the consequence of a rising dollar... Today's movement (yesterday) stresses that global markets and institutions will have to get used to a yuan that will be more governed by market forces and the greater volatility that entails."\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war?At the analyst level there is the fear that this will stoe a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war. "The refusal to allow for more intense depreciation is largely due to the fear of unleashing greater capital outflows. China is also aware that the \uc2 US government\uc2  is looking up at the exchange rate, with a President Trump who is still complaining about the strength of the dollar," says Oxford Economics. If Trump and the Fed try to weaken the dollar, a global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war can break out.\par \par \uc2 Hao Zhou\uc2 , a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Commerzbank, points out that "the implications of overstepping the area of seven yuan for every dollar are tremendous. We will see a new wave of depreciations in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and risk-off sentiment could go further in global markets. In conclusion, we are facing a mess in the markets."\par \par \uc2 China's entry dropped the yuan at lows since 2008 in response to the new US tariff barrier was first published in The Third.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020190806ef86001pl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
