\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The curious story of the "swap" with China for $18.6 billion\b0\par\par\uc2 924 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 By Carlos Burgue\u241\'00\'F1ocburgueno@ambito.com.arYesterday's devaluation of yesterday's yuan resulted in an automatic and unwelcome loss of about $519 million for the country. The obligatory position in the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the result of the successive "swaps" that the country has renewed since 2014, made a third of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves currently nominated in this \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and, therefore, there were unintended consequences on assets financial institutions. In total, until Friday, the nominated amount in yuan reached $18.6 billion, money that yesterday fell 1.3% without anything can be done from Buenos Aires to prevent it. Likewise, because of the way it is designed, it is still a more than useful mechanism to show the market, since for the entity that manages \uc2 Guido Sandleris\uc2  it is a financial asset of free availability. That is, you could use them at the right time to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local exchange rate market.\par \par \uc2  While since April 29, the BCRA has more oiled and effective tools (the $9 billion enabled by the \uc2 IMF\uc2 ), the Chinese swap weapon is always in place.\par \par \uc2 Like almost all monetary agreements reached by the country, the enabling of this instrument is also controversial. A "swap" is a mechanism by which Argentina and \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  undertake to eventually enable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange, without the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of third \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; in this case, the dollar. The capital contribution is made by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of China\uc2 , under the certainty that the original yuan will eventually be used. In the meantime, until the change is executed, they remain as free availability of the depositor: the BCRA. The Chinese idea was to grant this money in installments, as collateral for the financial exchange between the two countries for the construction of the great works in the country committed to the Asian country; mainly the Condor Cliff Dam (former Cepernic-Kirchner); a project that the Government of \uc2 Mauricio Macri\uc2  once promised to close but which, precisely because of the validity of the "swap" decided to keep in force.\par \par \uc2 The first such agreement was signed in 2009 during Martin Redrado's presidency at the BCRA, to reinforce the shelters in the face of possible international crises and when the reserves reached the record of 15% of GDP. In total the closed agreement was for about US$10.2 billion to threeyears, with the option of extending the deadline. Redrado negotiated it with his Chinese peer, \uc2 Zhou Xiaochuan\uc2 , to arrange a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange that both countries could order from each other and which should then be repaid. The operating permits for the BCRA were extensive. Yuan could be converted into dollars into international markets, or directly used for bilateral exchange. Or, failing that, keep them as part of the reserves nominated in the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . However, over time, the instrument began to blur.\par \par \uc2 The second movement with China was activated in the third quarter of 2014,during the management of \uc2 Axel Kicillof\uc2  in Economics and \uc2 Juan Carlos F\u225\'00\'E1brega\uc2  in the BCRA, for about US$3.8 billion, transferred in the last quarter of that year. The novelty of this \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  was that it was justified under the beginning of the works for the lifting of the Cepernic-Kirchner Santacruce dam that the Chinese construction company Gezouba had won in partnership with the local Cordoba Electroengineering. The total agreement was for about US$11 billion, in successive settlements dependent on the progress of the works. During the first half of 2015, a new disbursement was made for about US$3.7 billion, completing up to that point a total of US$6.5 billion. The money fromChina had come at a fair time to support the last stretches of \uc2 Cristina Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez de Kirchner\uc2 's government, when the lack of dollars and ostracism in international markets was already worrying. Reserves were around US$30 billion, and Argentina's ability to use international financial markets at reasonable rates was zero. The swap renewal agreement with China came at an ideal time to be able to sustain reserves and cope with eventual runs before the end of the Kirchnergovernment government. By the end of 2014, about $3 billion of the deal had already been used. In fact, about $2 billion from this funding was used to cancel the Boden 2015 final payment.Then came the change of government, and the decision of \uc2 Mauricio Macri\uc2  to revise Gezhouba's contract to build the dam still called Cepernic- Kirchner. The first public decision of the current Government was to freeze the work, on suspicion of corruption and negative environmental impact. However, by July 2016, from Beijing they reminded Buenos Aires that some of the money for the work had already been spent (and not precisely to move forward with the dam), so that if the project was lifted, the money had to be returned. Thus, the swap conditions were "renegotiated"; the work came back to life under another name (later called Condor Cliff), and the swap would be reactivated. The mechanism was renewed for about $11 billion with a term of three more years, bringing them to yuan to about $8 billion. Last year it was renegotiated with Luis Caputo at the head of the BCRA, with a further disbursement of us$10 billion, money that is now the one that reinforces the reserves of the BCRA, despite yesterday's devaluation. At the moment it is not intended for the work of Santa Cruz, which is basically paralyzed.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020190806ef86000y3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
