\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Countervailing quota validity review imposed on steel chain imports of welded links originating in China\b0\par\par\uc2 28,502 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juli 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 DOF: 17/07/2019\par \par \uc2 RESOLUTION Final review of the countervailing quota imposed on steel chain imports of welded links originating in the People's Republic of China, regardless of the country of origin.\par \par \uc2 Download PDF\par \par \par \par \uc2 On the sidelines a stamp with the National Shield, which says: United Mexican States.- Secretariat of economy.\par \par \uc2 FINAL RESOLUTION OF THE EXAMINATION OF THE VIGENCE OF THE COMPENSATORY SHARE IMPOSED ON STEEL CHAIN IMPORTS OF WELDED SLABONS ORIGINATING IN THE POPULAR REPUBLIC CHINA, INDEPENDENTLY OF THE COUNTRY OF PROCEDENCE Seen to resolve in the final stage of the administrative file E.C. 09/18 based in the International Trade Practices Unit of the Secretariat of the Economy (the "Secretariat"), this Resolution is issued in accordance with the following RESULTING A. Final Resolution of the investigation anti-dumping 1. On 17 July 2003, the Final Resolution of the Anti-Dumping Investigation on Steel Chain Imports of Welded Links originating in the People's Republic of China ("China"), was published in the Official Journal of the Federation (DOF) country of origin (the "Final Resolution of the Anti-Dumping Investigation"). By this Resolution, the Secretariat determined a final countervailing fee of 0.72 United States dollars ("dollars") per kilogram to final and temporary imports, including those entering under the eighth rule of the implementation of the General Import and Export Taxes Act (TIGIE) Tariff. B. Previous Term Exams 2. On 5 January 2010, the Final Resolution of the first review of the compensatory quota was published in the DOF. It was determined to modify the compensatory quota from $0.72 to $0.50 per kilogram and keep it in effect for five more years. 3. On 21 July 2014, the Final Resolution of the second review of the compensatory quota was published in the DOF. It was determined to keep it in force for five more years, in the terms of the previous point. C. Notice on the validity of compensatory quotas 4. On 7 November 2017, the Notice on the validity of compensatory quotas was published in the DOF. Domestic producers and any person with legal interest were hereby informed that the final countervailing quotas imposed on the products listed in that Notice would be eliminated from the expiry date indicated in the each, unless a domestic producer expressed in writing its interest in the initiation of an examination procedure. The list included the welded-link steel chain originating in China, which was the subject of this review. D. Manifestation of Interest 5. On June 12, 2018, Deacero, S.A.P.I. de C.V. ("Deacero") and Industrial de Alambres, S.A. de C.V. ("Industrial de Alambres") expressed an interest in the Secretariat initiating the review of the validity of the countervailing quota. E. Resolution initiating the third review of the validity of the countervailing quota 6. On 16 July 2018, the Secretariat published in the DOF the Resolution declaring the beginning of the review of the countervailing quota imposed on steel chain imports of welded links originating in China (the "Initiation Resolution"). The review period was set from 1 April 2017 to 31 March 2018 and as an analysis period from 1 April 2013 to 31 March 2018. F. Product under review 1. Product Description 7. The product under examination is a carbon steel wire product, cut, bent and welded to form the chain. It is known by the generic steel chain name of welded links,although it also has the following names: welded chain, polished chain, galvanized chain, electro-galvanized chain, electro-welded chain or welded link chain. 8. The main characteristics identifying the chain under examination are the diameter of the wire forming the links, the length and width of the links, the resistance to the stress (workload and rupture) and the weight per linear meter. 9. The diameter of the wire is relevant in the purchasing decision of consumers, as it influences the tensile strength of the chain. The most common wire diameters are 1/8, 3/16, 1/4, 5/16, 3/8, 7/16, 1/2 and 1 inch. To some degree, the various diameters can be interchangeable with each other, depending on the stress resistance they have and the safety factor required. In general, the chain can be marketed interchangeably polished or galvanized with zinc (except in uses where corrosion resistance is important). 2. Tariff treatment 10. The product under review enters the domestic market by tariff fraction 7315.82.02 of the TIGIE, the description of which is as follows:Tariff codingDescriptionChapter 73Casting, iron or steel manufactures.Game 7315Chains and their parts, cast iron or steel.\u160\'00\'A0\u8211\'20\'13 Other chains:Subheading 7315.82\u8212\'20\'14 The other chains, of welded links.Fraction 7315.82.02Weight less than 15 Kg per linear meter, extended, except for the fraction 7315.82.01.Source: Internet Tariff Information System (SIAVI). 11. The unit of measure used by TIGIE is the kilogram, although in commercial \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  tubs or 50 kilogram coasts are used. 12. In accordance with SIAVI and the Decree amending TIGIE, as well as the Decree establishing various Sectoral Promotion Programmes, published in DOF on 9 February 2010, imports entering by tariff fraction 7315.82.0 2 of the TIGIE were exempt from the tariff as of 1 January 2012, whatever their origin. 3. Production process 13. The supplies used to manufacture the welded link steel chain are the wire rod, and the zinc when the final product was galvanized. Other raw materials include electric power, labor and specialized machinery. 14. Generally speaking, the production process begins with the trefilation of the wire rod in 1, 3 and 4 step stretching machines. The resulting wire is cleaned with tungsten carbide dice (mechanical pickling) and spun into reels or trolls that pass into a machine, where the wire is cut to form the links, which are hooked to form the chain. 15. The links are sold by electric arc. The steel chain undergoes various tests to verify that it meets the given length, weld quality, and minimum load specified by the standards. The steel chain is polished or galvanized with zinc by immersion or through electro galvanized processes. Finally, the steel chain is weighed and packed in 25- or 50-kilogram plastic buckets, mainly, or in sacks of different weights. 4. Standards 16. The product under review complies with the standards of the \uc2 American Society for Testing and Materials\uc2  (ASTM), ASTM, A-413/A-413M-00 (Specification for Steel Chain at National Association of Chain Manufacturers (NACM). 5. Uses and functions 17. The steel chain of welded links hasvarious uses. Domestic employment is the most common, for example, to close house or retail bars, prevent passage in parking lots and restrict the movement of goods or animals. In the agricultural sector it is used to tow crops and sawmills to move or knock down logs and keep them fixed in the contenders where they are transported. In the transport industry, to tow all kinds of vehicles and, in construction, to load various materials. It is also used on shrimp boats to hold the net with which the shrimp are caught. 18. Some market segments prefer the galvanized chain because it offers greater resistance to oxidation and has a better physical appearance, but can be replaced by polished chain without undermining its functions, especially when prices are favorable. The markets and consumers of each steel chain are pretty much the same. G. Call and Notifications 19. By the publication of the Initiation Resolution, the Secretariat convened domestic producers, importers, exporters and any person who considered to have a legal interest in the outcome of this review, to appear to present the arguments and evidence that they considered relevant. 20. The Secretariat notified the parties of the knowledge of the initiation of the present proceedings and the Government of China. H. Composite Interested Parties 21. The proceedings were compared in a timely manner by the domestic producers: Deacero, S.A.P.I. de C.V. Av. Av. L\u225\'00\'E1zaro C\u225\'00\'E1rdenas No. 2333 Col. Valle Oriente C.P. 66269, San Pedro Garza Garc\u237\'00\'EDa, Nuevo Le\u243\'00\'F3n Industrial de Alambres, S.A. de C.V. Blvd. Captain Carlos Camacho Spirit No. 1501 Col. Barrio La Asunci\u243\'00\'F3n San Francisco Totimehuac\u225\'00\'E1n C.P. 72595, Puebla, Puebla I. Arguments and means of proof 1. Overtime 22. The Secretariat granted a fortnight extension to Deacero and Industria de Alambres to submit its response to the official form, as well as the arguments and evidence that were agreed upon by their right. The deadline expired on 13 September 2018. 2. Domestic producers a. Deacero 23. On 13 September 2018, Deacero stated: i. Aspects on the continuation or recurrence of dumping A.\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0The export price was obtained from the list of steel chain imports entered by tariff fraction 7315.82.02 of the TIGIE during the period investigated, provided by the National Chamber of the Iron and Steel Industry (CANACERO), with based on information from the Tax Administration Service (SAT). B. The export price for maritime freight, goods insurance, customs and port procedures in China and land freight in the interior of that country is adjusted. C. Since in Chinese industry, producer and exporter of the product under review, conditions prevail that do not reflect the principles of a market economy, it is proposed to calculate normal value based on the substitute country methodology. This, because of the following: (a) the Chinese government sets the exchange rate of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to reduce it and enhance its economy, orienting it to export markets, which prevents its value from being determined by market forces; b. the devaluation of the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  causes a decrease in the price of the steel wire rod, the main raw material of the product under review; c. wages are not established through free negotiation between workers and employers, since the legal framework is not effectively applied; there are also government policies that restrict the mobility of workers, which means that the cost of labour is not determined by the market; d. Accounting records are made with criteria that differ from the principlesgenerally accepted accounting, so there is little reliability in financial reporting; e. there are restrictions on foreign investment, such as the imposition of caps, merger requirements, an administrative approval system, conditional on technology transfer, and actions that disadvantage investors foreigners, such as pricing to enter the market; f. The Chinese Communist Party has party organizations within more than 70% of Chinese companies and in almost 91% of government-owned enterprises, including the energy and steel industry, and g.\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0decisions on prices, costs and supplies are made through government policies; the government also has stake and ownership of companies in strategic sectors, so it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly by providing credits, approving land use and providing financial support, for example: i. owns three of the main and has a stake in nine of the top ten steel producers in China, and ii.\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0has the stake and ownership of various companies producing wire rods, the main raw material of the product under review. It also implements policies that allow such companies to operate despite having financial problems, benefits that are passed on to the manufacturers of the product under review. D. The Chinese government interferes with the production factors of the product under review, as a result of the following: a. electricity prices, input of the product under review, are controlled by the State, so that the cost structure of the same n or may reflect its true cost, in addition to the preferential subsidies and tariffs granted; b. State-owned enterprises receive land-use rights without incurring any cost, or with subsidies from municipal governments; c. State-owned enterprises may purchase iron ore at subsidized prices, as the government restricts exports of such a product or invests in deposits outside China to support its steel industry, and d.\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0the costs of wire rod are distorted by the costs of electricity, labor, capital, iron ore, land use, as well as by the fact that producers have access to buy the billet, the predecessor raw material, below their fair market value. E. Brazil is proposed as a market economy country, a substitute for China, for the calculation of normal value, on account of the following: a. the price of the steel chain of welded links in that country is determined by the free participation of the bidders and market constituents. In addition, there are no restrictions on the entry or exit of the product, the companies are from the private sector and there are no price controls or quotas; b. it is clear from the most recent notification on subsidies submitted by the Brazilian government to the \uc2 World Trade Organization (WTO)\uc2 , that there is no government interference in the welded-link steel chain industry, as no reports are reported subsidies or other benefits for the steel industry; c. the cost structure of factors that are intensively used in production processes used in both China and Brazil, to produce welded-link steel chain, is similar. This, since the production process of both countries is carried out through the same stages, through the use of machinery and mature and similar technology, it is not labor intensive and uses the same supplies. In addition, the raw material is the main element of cost, and d.\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0both countriesare important producers of steel wire rod, based on the production process of the product under review. In addition, they have a vast local supply of energy, another important input in the production process of steel chain of welded links. F. To calculate the normal value, price references were obtained in the domestic market of Brazil, obtained from company quotes corresponding to more than 90% of the producers in that market, obtained from the study prepared by an indepe consultant n.d.' G.\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0It is proposed to adjust the price references used for the calculation of normal value by the concepts of taxes, volume discounts and inflation. H. Although China is considered to continue to behave as a non-market economy, it obtained as an alternative for the calculation of normal value price references in China's domestic market, from quotes from producing and marketing companies (s) steel chain of welded links in that country, obtained by the consultant UNO International Trade Strategy (UNO), which can be considered representative, since the productive capacity of the companies represents, for three of them, twice the capacity of the domestic industry, while two more companies have twice the annual revenue of the former, so it is assumed that its productive capacity is higher. I. Price references in China's domestic market obtained by Consultant UNO are expressed at the ex-factory level, so they do not require more adjustment than inflation. ii. Aspects of continuation or recurrence of damage J.\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0Despite the existence of the countervailing quota, the product under review entered the Mexican market during the analysis period, suggesting that, if the countervailing quota were eliminated, the unfair practice would be repeated. K:i.\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0The domestic market is and will remain attractive to exporters because of the expectations of growth in the Mexican economy from the second quarter of 2018 and 2019, as imports maintained their presence in the domestic market at despite the existence of a countervailing quota and given the commercial opening with respect to the product under review. L. During the period of validity of the countervailing quota, the structure of the domestic supply and demand of the product under review remained stable, highlighting only that in 2017 Truper, S.A. de C.V. ("Truper"), in addition to being an importer of the product under ex amen, began producing the domestically manufactured like. M.\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0Domestic industry prices decreased by approximately 15% during the period of the countervailing quota, in an environment in which imports of the product under review entered the national territory at unfair and lower prices nationals. N. The period of validity of the countervailing quota under consideration has not been sufficient to counter injury to the domestic industry, since conditions prevail ingentiously that place domestic industry in vulnerable condition, in accordance with the following.\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0domestic industry sales volume decreased by 5% in the review period and 13% in the review period; b. the volume of production of the domestic industry fell by 5% in the review period and 1% in the review period; c. the use of production capacity of the domestic industry reached levels of 53% on average; d. domestic industry sales prices show stagnation in the last year of the compensatory quota term, and e.\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0Deacero's operating profits recorded a fall inmore than 86% during the review period and 65% during the period analysed, financial fragility which would be due if the compensatory quota was eliminated. O. If the countervailing quota on steel chain imports of welded links were eliminated, the following effects would occur: a. Imports of the product under review would increase to a volume of 604,190 kilograms in the period of 2018-March 2019, and 1,198,870 in the period April 2019-March 2020. It is also estimated an increase in imports from other sources; b. Import prices of the product under review will decrease by 18% and 7% in the periods April 2018-March 2019 and April 2019-March 2020, respectively, relative to the prices they maintained during the review period. Import prices from other sources will also decline, however, they will continue to rise above domestic industry prices. In addition, the prices of national counterpart merchandise are expected to fall by 18% and 7%, respectively, during the periods referred to; c. the volume of sales of the domestic industry to the Mexican market will decrease by more than 9% and 19% in the periods April 2018-March 2019 and April 2019-March 2020, respectively, compared to the volume recorded in the review period, which will generate that the volume production in the domestic industry is declining by more than 26% and 35% in those periods, respectively, compared to the review period; d. Deacero's sales volume will decrease by more than 25% and 24% in the periods April 2018-March 2019 and April 2019-March 2020, respectively, in relation to the review period, and e.\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0Deacero's capacity utilization will fall by around 15-20 percentage points in the periods April 2018-March 2019 and April 2019-March 2020, respectively, compared to the review period. Q. China has a large productive capacity of the product under review, as the volume of its exports to the world increased by more than 12% from 2013 to 2017. The productive capacity of five Chinese producers is greater than 142 thousand tonnes, significantly higher than the productive capacity of domestic production. Q. China's vast export potential is reflected in its 88% share of world exports during 2017, supplying 84% on average of global demand. A. Welded chain exports worldwide decreased by more than 21 million kilograms when compared to the period April 2013-March 2014 vs. April 2017-March 2018, and recorded a decrease of 26 million kilograms in the review period , compared to the previous immediate, which could indicate that string consumption decreases globally. It is therefore clear that China will reorient its exports to othermarkets, such as Mexico, which is among the twelve major chain importers. S. Chinese industry's interest in markets in the \uc2 North American Free Trade Agreement\uc2  region is reflected in the growth of U.S. imports by 40% and Canadian imports by 13%, compared to the period April 2017-March 2018 with s or previous immediate counterpart, in addition to the decline of Chinese exports to the rest of the world by 3%. T. There are no international factors that have a direct and significant effect on domestic industry indicators, although export volumes in domestic industry decreased during the period March 2013-April 2014 in contrast to the March 2017-April 2018, it is also true that of the comparison of the review period with its counterpartprevious immediate notices a recovery of almost 40%. U. Apparent National Consumption (ANC) shows an upward trend of 5% during the analysis period, compared from start to finish, so negative effects on national industry indicators cannot be attributed to a decrease in consumption in the competition with imports of the product under review under unfair conditions. 24. Deacero submitted: A. Export price to Mexico of the welded link steel chain originating in China, for the review period, adjustments and worksheet for the calculation of the same. B. Information on inflation in China, from March to July 2018, obtained from the website inflation.eu, accessed on 28 August 2018, and worksheet for the monthly inflation calculation from March to July 2018. C. Normal value in the domestic market of China and Brazil, with their respective adjustments. D. Quotes from various Chinese producers of the product under review, with description of diameter, finish, price per kilogram and average, obtained by consultant UNO. E. Stainless Alloy Steel Chain Quotes obtained from the \uc2 alibaba.com\uc2  website, as well as an email of 15 August 2018, sent by staff of Nantong New Jianghai International Trade Co., Ltd. F.\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0Academic and work profile of the UNO consultant, obtained from his website. G.\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0Market study of welded steel chains in Brazil, prepared by independent consultant Boaventura d'Avila, August 2018. H. Information on the steel industry in Brazil, obtained from the website of the Brazilian Steel Institute, consulted on 23 August 2018. I. Information on industrial relations in Brazil, obtained from the website {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.deloitte.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.deloitte.com}}}\uc2 , accessed on August 30, 2018. J. Circular of the Ministry of Industry and Technology Information for The Development and National Reform of the Government of China, concerning the use of prices as a means to promote structural reform in the supply of the iron and steel industry, of December 30, 2016, obtained from the website {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.gov.cn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf