vailing quota, Industrial de Alambres operated in a context of contraction of thedomestic market, so it experienced a deterioration in its economic and \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  variables, especially in domestic production and sales, with a lag in domestic sales prices at the cost-of-sale level, and the consequent financial impact placed on the vulnerable to the possible reduction or elimination of the countervailing quota. B. The countervailing quota was not sufficient to eliminate unfair practice, as Chinese steel chain imports at discriminated prices and below Industrial's domestic sales prices of Wires, however, imported volumes were limited by the application of that measure. C. In the period April 2013-March 2018, the production volume of Industria de Alambres decreased by 42% and its sales volume to the domestic market fell by 40%, so that its participation in the ANC contracted by 20 percentage points , while its productive idle capacity increased by this same amount during the examination period. D. The increase in sales prices to the internal market of Industria de Alambres, during the period of the compensatory quota, was not reflected in its revenue from domestic sales, as these were reduced by 32% as a result of the lower volume of vents a. This price increase lagged against the increased unit production costs that increased, so the company's operating performance showed a reduction. E. In a countervailing scenario, in the two projected periods following the review period, imports of the product under review shall enter with significant margins of undervaluation which, in the event of a possible reduction or elimination of the compensatory quota shall incentivise the entry of such product at levels close to that recorded prior to the application of the countervailing quota. F. In the face of a countervailing quota elimination scenario, the following is foreseen for Industria de Alambres: a. the deterioration of its fragile \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  circumstance in the face of the entry of the product under review at reduced prices and with respe undercutting margins national prices; b. its prices shall be around the estimated low prices of Chinese imports in the two periods following the review period, with the margin of undercutting narrowing with the prices offered to the domestic market, and c.\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0potential Chinese chain imports would reach a volume that would lead to a substantial increase in their share of the ANC, with the share of domestic production being withthe interest in domestic production in these periods. G.\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0Imports of the product under review will have negative impacts on Wire Industry indicators, such as sales, production volume, participation in the ANC, utilization of installed capacity, employment, sales prices and revenue per domestic sales. H. In a countervailing (sic) scenario, the prices of Chinese steel chain imports will be below Industrial de Wire's domestic selling prices, with estimated undercutting margins over the projected periods. I. In a scenario without a countervailing fee, the diminished operating gain obtained during the period of the compensatory quota would turn to irrecoverable losses, which will inevitably imply the irreversible closure of Industrial's \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wires. 26. Industrial Wire presented: A. Value and volume of total and specific steel chain imports of welded links, originating in China and the rest of the world, entered through thetariff fraction 7315.82.02 of the TIGIE in the period 2013-2018, with projections for the periods 2018-2019 and 2019-2020, in scenarios with and without countervailing quota. B. Indicators of the domestic welded link steel chain and Wire Industry industry, consisting of value and volume of sales to the domestic 