res and Deacero, respectively, to submit their response to the Secretariat's request for information on 31 October 2018. The deadlines expired on 3 and 17 December 2018, respectively. 29. The Secretariat granted a ten-day extension to Deacero and Industria de Alambres to submit its response to the Request for Information made by the Secretariat on 20 February 2019. The deadline expired on 21 March 2019. 2. Domestic producers a. Deacero 30. On 31 October 2018, the Secretariat requested Deacero to, inter alia, introduce a new purification methodology to identify imports of the product under review; provide information on the concepts it proposed as adjustments to export price and normal value; demonstrate that in the production and sale of welded link steel chain in China, cost and price structures prevail that are not determined according to market principles; justify the relevance of price references in Brazil; credit the participation of the producer companies contained in the UNO consultant's quote in its domestic market; justify the use of imports reported by UN Comtrade for the calculation of the growth rate of steel chain imports into Mexico; present the methodology and criteria applied in its estimation of market share and installed capacity; correct their domestic sales projections; explains the methodology used to project the wage mass, why it used indirect employment to project its productivity, and why its productivity projections do not match the estimate presented; justify why it considered, for total steel chain exports of Chinese welded links, non-subject product, correct the conversion factor and clarify the period for which it projected industry indicators of the exporting country ; provide various clarifications on the information included in its cost, sales and profits status of domestic ally-oriented domestic goods; define the reference values or variables you used for your financial projections and make sure that your projections were consistent;