\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Anti-dumping investigation on imports of aluminium pressure cookers originating in China\b0\par\par\uc2 19,209 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 On the sidelines a stamp with the National Shield, which says: United Mexican States.- Secretariat of economy.\par \par \uc2 PRELIMINARY RESOLUTION OF THE ANTIDUMPING INVESTIGATION ON THE IMPORTS OF ALUMINIUM PRESSURE OLLAS ORIGINAL TO THE POPULAR REPUBLIC CHINA, INDEPENDENTLY OF THE COUNTRY OF PROCEDENCE Seen to resolve the file at the preliminary stage 12/18 located in the International Trade Practices Unit (UPCI) of the Secretariat of the Economy (the "Secretariat"), this Resolution is issued in accordance with the following RESULTING A. Application 1. On 7 August 2018, Grupo Vasconia, S.A.B. ("Vasconia" or the "Applicant"), requested the initiation of the administrative investigation for unfair international trade practices, in its form of price discrimination, on imports of pots of aluminium pressure up to 9 liters capacity, originating in the People's Republic of China ("China"), regardless of the country of origin. B. Initiation of research 2. On 20 December 2018, the Resolution initiating the anti-dumping investigation (the "Initiation Resolution") was published in the Official Journal of the Federation (DOF). The period of investigation was fixed from 1 May 2017 to 30 April 2018, and as a damage analysis period from 1 May 2015 to 30 April 2018. C. Product under investigation 1. Overview 3. The product under investigation is aluminum pressure cookers up to 9 liters capacity, usually for domestic use ("aluminum pressure cookers"). 4. The trade name with which the product under investigation is known is aluminum pressure cookers up to 9 liters capacity or aluminium express cookers up to 9 liters capacity. 2. Features 5. The product under investigation are aluminium containers intended for rapid cooking of food with capacity up to 9 liters, so they are considered for domestic use, with adjustable aluminum lid and rubber packaging, which withstand pressures inside. Its capacity ranges from 2 to 9 liters and withstand a pressure of between 50 and 90 kilopascales. 6. The essential characteristics that allow the product under investigation to be identified are the aluminium material of the body and cap, and which are composed of four main parts: (i) body or base with capacity up to 9 liters; ii) lid adjustable to pot body; (iii) pressure regulator and safety valve, and iv) handles and handles. They may include other components such as pressure indicator and other safety devices. 3. Tariff treatment 7. The product under investigation enters the domestic market through tariff fraction 7615.10.01 of the Tariff of the General Import and Export Taxes Act (TIGIE), the description of which is as follows:\par \par \uc2 Tariff codingDescriptionChapter 76Aluminum and aluminum manufactures.Game 7615Household items, hygiene or vanity and their parts, aluminum; sponges, scouring pads, gloves and similar articles for scrubbing, polishing or similar uses, of aluminum.Subheading 7615.10\u8211\'20\'13 Household items and their parts; sponges, scouring pads, gloves and similar items for scrubbing, polishing or similar uses.Fraction 7615.10.01Pressure cooker.Source: Internet Tariff Information System (SIAVI). 8. According to SIAVI, imports of the investigated goods entering by tariff fraction 7615.10.01 of the TIGIE is subject to an ad val\u243\'00\'F3rem tariff of 15%, with the exception of Panama with a preferential tariff of 7.5%, in force at 31December 2019, Mexico's countries with which Mexico has concluded free trade agreements are duty-free. 9. The unit of measure used in TIGIE and commercial \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the kilogram. 4. Production process 10. The main inputs for the manufacture of the product under investigation are: aluminum discs for the body and lid of the pot, components for the body and lid (plastic or Bakelite handles and handles, safety valve, pressure regulator and packaging) and packaging) and Electricity. The manufacturing process of the product under investigation consists of the following stages: a. prepared from the aluminium disc: raw materials are received and inspected, in particular the aluminium disc that serves as the base of the pot and lid, as well as the rest or inputs (handles and handles, rivets and other accessories, labels, plates and instructions, pressure regulators, rubber packaging and boxes); b. Base die-cutting: the body of the pot is molded using lubricants; c. grinding and washing: the lashes are perforated to close with the lid tightly; cleans and polishes the pot, and pierces to put the handles; d. die-cutting lid: molds and perforates the lid to insert the handle and valve and attachments; e. polishing and polishing: polishing of the pot body, and polishing and polishing of the pot lid; f. assembly: the valve is placed with nuts and bolts and handles; a plastic package is then placed on the lid so that it closes tightly with the pot, and g.\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0packaging: The instructions for use, labels and packed are placed. 5. Standards 11. Aluminum pressure cookers must comply in Mexico with The Official Mexican Standard NOM-054-SCFI-1998, Household utensils-Pressure-Safety. 6. Uses and functions 12. The main use and function of aluminum pressure cookers is the rapid cooking of food by pressure inside, usually for domestic use. D. Call and Notifications 13. By the Initiation Resolution, the Secretariat convened the importers and exporters of the product under investigation and any person who considered to have a legal interest in the outcome of the investigation, to appear to present the arguments and evidence that they considered relevant. 14. The Secretariat notified the applicant, the importers and exporters available to the applicant and the Government of China of the initiation of the anti-dumping investigation. With the notification, they had the transfer of the public version of the request for initiation, the response to the prevention and their respective annexes, as well as the official investigative forms, in order to make their defence. E. Interested Parties Composed 15. No interested party appeared, so the only party accredited in the proceeding is the Applicant: 1. Applicant Company Grupo Vasconia, S.A.B. Av. Insurgentes Sur No. 1898 Siglum Tower Building, floor 14, office 1421 Col. Florida C.P. 01020, Ciudad Mexico F. Information Requirements 1. Overtime 16. The Secretariat granted Vasconia an extension of ten working days and four working days to a customs agent to submit its response to the requests made by the Secretariat on 7 March 2019. The deadlines expired on 29 March and 5 April 2019, respectively. 2. Interested Parties a. Applicant 17. On 7 March 2019, the Secretariat requested Vasconia to, inter alia, explain the difference and correct the inconsistency in its figures on installed capacity and production volume in China; provide re-data from the exporting country's industry indicators for aluminium pressure cookers for the period analyzed,if it does not have specific information, it will provide it to the next level of aggregation and, if any of the indicators are estimated, explain the methodology and present the worksheets and documentary support, and provide the status of costs, sales and domestic sales profits of similar merchandise for the periods May 2015-April 2016, May 2016-April 2017, and May 2017-April 2018. The deadline expired on April 5, 2019. 3. No Parts 18. On 7 and 8 March 2019, the Secretariat requested a number of customs agents to submit import edise and their accompanying documentation. The deadlines expired on 21 and 25 March 2019. G. Other appearances 19. On 18 February 2019, the exporting companies Alegacy Foodservice Products Groupe Inc. and Dorian Drake International Inc. appeared to state that they did not export the product under investigation. CONSIDERING A. Competition 20. The Secretariat is competent to issue this Resolution, in accordance with Articles 16 and 34 fractions V and XXXIII of the Organic Law of the Federal Public Administration; 1, 2 paragraph B fraction III and 15 fraction I of the Internal Regulations of the Secretariat of the Economy; 7, 9.1 and 12.2 of the Agreement on the Implementation of Article VI of the General Agreement on Tariffs and Trade 1994 (the "Anti-Dumping Agreement"); 5 fraction VII and 57 fraction I of the Foreign Trade Act (LCE), and 80 and 82 fraction I of the Regulations of the Foreign Trade Act (RLCE). B. Applicable Law 21. For purposes of this procedure, the Anti-Dumping Agreement, the LCE, the RLCE, the Federation Tax Code (CFF), the Federal Law on Administrative Litigation Procedure and the Federal Code of Civil Procedure, the latter three of the Application. C. Protection of Confidential Information 22. The Secretariat may not publicly disclose the confidential information submitted to it by interested parties or the confidential information provided upon it, in accordance with Articles 6.5 of the AD Agreement, 80 of the LCE and 152 and 158 of the RLCE. However, interested parties may obtain access to confidential information, provided that they satisfy the requirements set out in Articles 159 and 160 of the RLCE. D. Rights of defence and due process 23. Stakeholders had ample opportunity to present all kinds of arguments, exceptions and defences, as well as evidence to support them, in accordance with the AD Agreement, the LCE and the RLCE. The Secretariat assessed them subject to the essential formalities of the administrative procedure. E. Price Discrimination Analysis 24. At this stage of the investigation, the Secretariat had no arguments or evidence from importing companies, exporting producers or the Chinese government, and made its determination based on the facts available to it, in terms of what it Articles 6.8 and Annex II of the Anti-Dumping Agreement and 54 and 64 of the LCE. These facts correspond to the information and evidence submitted by Vasconia, as well as, as well as, as well as, as the information that the Secretariat itself had been granted. 1. Export price 25. The Applicant calculated the export price from import statistics for tariff fraction 7615.10.01 of the TIGIE, whereby the aluminium pressure cookers entered during the period investigated, data it obtained from the Tax Administration Service (SAT). However, by the tariff fraction it entered a product other than the one investigated, so it identified those records according to the description of each \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . 26. The products he excluded were pressure cookers with capacities greater than 9 litres, pans, minipanel, sets of aluminum containers for laboratory tests, aluminum lids, aluminum kitchen vessel for popcorn and steel pressure cookers, electric, programmable, for cooking rice and for polymerization of dental sections. 27. For those \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  that the product description did not report the capacity of the aluminum pressure cookers, the Applicant used the following criteria: a. when the description contains the model, it identified the capability through a search in Internet; b. where the description contains the mark, after a search on the internet it identified that that mark only markets aluminium pressure cookers with capacities greater than or less than 9 litres; c. identified importers that market only specific capacities, i.e. less than 9 litres or greater than 9 litres; d. the specific description that it is an industrial pressure cooker; e. the records in which he failed to identify the capacity, used the weight-by-piece criterion. Vasconia identified as aluminum pressure cookers less than 9 liters those records that on average their weight was less than 6 kg/piece and as aluminum pressure cookers greater than 9 liters those whose weight was greater than 6 kg/piece, and f.\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0in order not to overestimate the volume, it excluded those imports whose capacity was not identified. 28. For its part, the Secretariat drew on the list of imports of the investigated product originating in China, which it obtained through the Commercial Information System of Mexico (SIC-M). It matched this information against the import base provided by the Applicant, including the description, dollar value and volume. 29. The Secretariat determined to calculate the export price, on the basis of the SIC-M statistics, whereby the \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  contained in that database are obtained after validation of the customs orders that occur in a framework of exchange of information between customs agents and agents on the one hand and the customs authority on the other, which are reviewed by the \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2 . 30. At this stage of the investigation, the Secretariat requested import requests and accompanying documentation from various customs agents. The revision of this documentation allowed him to obtain information to identify the product under investigation and the capacity of aluminium pots denominated in litres. From the latter, it classified the aluminum pressure cookers into 6 categories, with capacities of 4.5, 5, 6, 7, 8 and 9 liters. 31. Based on Articles 39 and 40 of the RLCE, the Secretariat calculated a dollar-weighted average export price per kilogram for each of the six categories of the product under investigation. a. Adjustments to export price 32. Vasconia proposed to adjust the export price by terms and conditions of sale, specifically for the concepts of freight and domestic insurance in China and freight and maritime insurance. i. Inter