he goods investigated in China's domestic market, in accordance with Articles 33 of the LCE and 48 of the RLCE, as well as subparagraph (a) romanite (i) of paragraph 15 of China's Protocol of Accession to the WTO, pursuant to the Secretariat's found that the vasts and evidence provided by Vasconia indicate possible government \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  affecting macroeconomic variables, as well as the performance of the aluminium industry, as noted below: a. RMB is not freely convertible, by the strict controls by the Chinese government on capital outflows and inflows. The Secretariat noted that according to the information provided by the Applicant in the AREAR report published by the IMF, the restrictions imposed by countries on various capital market transactions and instruments are identified, pointing out China maintains restrictions on 11 of the 12 categories; b. foreign investment and co-investments are restricted by the State. According to information from the Catalogue to guide foreign investment in 2017, the aluminum industry is classified as a "encouraged" industry, and incentives are granted, including tax benefits; however, China's foreign investment regime remains one of the most restrictive in the world under the OECD Regulatory Restriction Index. Specifically, in the value chain of the product under investigation, state participation continues directly or through State-Owned Enterprises (SOE), as is the case with \uc2 Chinalco\uc2 , allowing infer the impact of price and cost formation of the investigated product through public policies or direct government participation; c. the cost of capital is distorted in China, on the grounds that the government keeps low the cost of raising capital used to finance loans, issue bonds and stocks. This as a result of maintaining lax risk premiums, as well as a very low ceiling on deposit rates, which are below the inflation rate. The executive summary: Evaluation of the legal framework of the regulatory legal framework and the policies that regulate the Chinese economy and its impact on the international competition carried out by think! DESK notes that in Chinese capital markets, prices are subject to government-induced distortions, mainly due to the pressure of interest rates and exchange rate manipulation; d. the cost of labour is distorted by policy restricting labour mobility through the Hukou family registry. By not granting the benefits derived from registration, companies could use labor at a lower cost, not having to cover the salary that a worker would have under the Hukou system.According to the document "What should economists know about the current Chinese hukuo system?", by Yang Song, published in China Economic Review 29, one-third of the workforce is migrant so they do not qualify for system benefits; (e) the cost of land is distorted, as a result of land rights for industrial use being arbitrarily allocated by the government. Real estate markets in China have high degrees of distortion, according to the company THINK! Desk. The document notes that prices for commercial land-use rights are pushed upwards by local governments to generate greater utility in land sales, while land for industrial use has decreased in price. Also, as a result of the allocation of land in China, industrial business models that require large tracts of land at a lower price are favored; f. the cost of energy is distorted, by China's price control. According to China's 2017 Analysis of Market Distortions in China's non-ferrous metals industry, energy support stands out for its large magnitude. Between 2011 and 2015, the 65 state-owned enterprises in the non-ferrous metals sector (including the aluminium industry) received total support of RMB2,083 million for electricity; G.\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the aluminium industry, through regional and five-year plans. The Secretariat noted that the Anhui Plan sought to expand aluminium production capacity and expand industrial chains for the manufacture of aluminium products, such as aluminum pressure cookers. For its part, the Five-Year Plan for the Aluminum Industry establishes restrictions on industrial entry, a situation that may have the purpose of maintaining an adequate profitability for existing companies, as argued by the Applicant. In addition, government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the aluminium sector is not only seen in government plans, but through various instruments such as direct cash donations, capital infusions and support that have reduced the cost of energy, as noted by the consulting firm THINK! DESK; h. state-owned aluminum-producing enterprises that benefit from various fiscal stimulus and support from the Chinese government. Based on the information contained in the Analysis of Market Distortions In China's 2017 Non-Ferrous Metals Industry, the Secretariat noted that the report contains a specific analysis of the aluminum industry in which it notes that the advantage in the sector is due to factors such as: (a) supports and loans that have enabled significant capital investments in large-scale production plants and advanced technology; b) low operating costs that the industry has because land, electricity, water, raw materials have a lower market value; (c) government supports identified in the integration of coal mining and power generation, and d) excess energy in western China, as well as differentiated prices in electricity tariffs; i. with regard to Chalco's pricing policies, the Secretariat considered that as an SOE, the operating conditions differed from private companies, as they usually do not have a profit-maximizing objective but of revenue that incentivizes expansion of its market. The absence of a budget constraint allows you to overinvest in installed capacity expansions and underestimate your production costs; j. because of theSOE's operates under prerogatives and benefits that private companies do not have even in unregulated sectors, so following international benchmarks in their pricing does not imply that centralised distortion in its production costs will be eliminated, in this sense, the price benchmark for such companies should be located above the cost level governing a profit-maximizing private company; K:i.\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0in addition, it is necessary to consider China's influence on the aluminium market as the world's largest producer, with the world's largest SOE's producers on an individual basis, so that the distorting effects of its domestic market are they move to the international arena, not only through oversupply but via depressed costs that are not determined under market economy conditions, and l.\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0there are export and refund tariffs on Value Added Tax (VAT) for primary aluminium. At this point, the same THINK! DESK notes that China exports little raw aluminium, but supplies semi-finished and finished aluminium products to the world. Trade policy in that country discourages the export of raw materials and primary aluminium, but encourages sales of higher value-added products. The report notes that exporting by-products instead of raw aluminum means that exporters can avoid paying a 30% tariff and claim a 15% VAT refund. 48. In this context, the Secretariat found that the aluminium sector could be affected by a wide range of government interference, such as the delivery of public policy programmes and supports, direct government \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , restrictions on foreign trade, capital and energy costs, as well as restrictions on labour mobility. In addition, in addition to the government's policy of promoting the manufacture of higher value-added aluminium products, all \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  could lead to price distortions in the latter, which is relevant in the present case, considering the distortion that may exist in the production chain of the product under investigation as the state-owned \uc2 Chinalco\uc2 , controlling shareholder of Chalco, China's main aluminium producer, and Henan Aluminium, which produces the aluminum discs, which is the main input of aluminum pressure cookers. 49. It can therefore be inferred that \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Chinese central government affect the aluminium pressure cooker industry in China by not reflecting market conditions because the cost of production of the product under investigation could be affected by "upstream" distortions. 50. Based on the information available in the administrative record, the Secretariat considers that they have sufficient elements to determine that in companies producing aluminium pressure cookers in China, cost and price structures that do not are determined according to market principles. Accordingly, in accordance with Articles 33 of the EcTE and 48 of the RLCE, as well as subparagraph (a) romanite (i) of paragraph 15 of China's Protocol of Accession to the WTO, the Secretariat determined to use a market-economy country of China for ef calculation of the normal value. c. Substitute country 51. Vasconia proposed to Brazil as China's substitute market economy country in this research, noting that Brazil is a market economy as WTO member countries are market economies as long as it is not determined otherwise, both in its protocols as in their respective WTO trade policy reviews. 52. He noted thatBrazil is a market open to foreign direct investment and promotes it in all sectors of its economy. In addition, the objectives of that country's trade policy have been to integrate global value chains and to increase competitiveness in its domestic products. In addition, the commitment to the multilateral trading system and its active participation. He supported his argument with the WTO Secretariat Report of Brazil's seventh Trade Policy Review of June 2017. 53. Brazil added that Brazil was among the ten economies in the world thanks to its natural resources, a strong industrial base and domestic market, diversified economic activity and a growing share of services in Gross Domestic Product. On the other hand, Brazil was committed to providing a transparent and open environment for international investment and competition in its market. In addition, transparency, predictability and due process in the facilitation of commerce is ensured, in accordance with the document "Active with Brazil", consulted on the website {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.oecd.org"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.oecd.org}}}\uc2 . i. Similarity in the production process 54. To support the production of the investigated goods in Brazil, Vasconia submitted a list of producers of the investigated goods in the proposed substitute country, also provided a list of pressure cookers originating in Brazil and pot quotes from manufactured by Brazilian companies, as well as by Chinese companies. 55. He noted that the production processes of the investigated product are similar in China and Brazil, which consist of various stages such as: obtaining the main input, die-cutting of aluminum, grinding, washing the pot and lid, polishing, polishing and finally the assembly and packaging process of the finished product. To support his argument, he provided information from a technical dossier for the manufacture of the investigated merchandise he obtained from the 2007 Brazilian Technical Response Service, and for the case of China provided links to Internet pages showing videos of the production processes of aluminum pressure cookers from Chinese manufacturers. ii. Availability of supplies 56. As for inputs, Vasconia noted that aluminum, electricity and labor stand out, of which both the country investigated and the substitute have access. For the case of aluminum in Brazil provided production figures per plant and installed capacity from 2014 to 2016, monthly production of aluminum for 2017 and 2018 and production figures of bauxite reserves, which it obtained from the Brazilian Aluminium Association. For China, it provided the report "Aluminium: Competitive Conditions Affecting the U.S. Industry", prepared by the \uc2 U.S. International Trade Commission\uc2 , which reports figures overproduction, imports, exports and availability of aluminium 2011 to 2015. 57. According to the 2017 country electricity production and consumption report, the 2017 Global Energy Statistical Yearbook, consulted on the website ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://yearbook.enerdata.net"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://yearbook.enerdata.net}}}\uc2 ), china is first found and Brazil in eighth place and ninth, respectively. For the workforce, Vasconia noted that China and Brazil have a significant workforce, in this regard, it submitted information from the website of the \uc2 U.S. Central Intelligence Agency\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.cia.gov"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.cia.gov}}}\uc2 ), which reports specific data on that country. iii. Other Elements 58. The Applicant noted that both China and Brazil have comparable economic development, supporting its argument with the 2017 Inclusive Growth and Development Report, issued by the \uc2 World Economic Forum\uc2 . He noted that both countries were classified in that document as high-middle-income economies due to theavailability of their resources, their growth and development processes at the inclusion level. iv. Determination 59. The second paragraph of Article 48 of the RLCE defines that a replacement country shall mean a third country with a market economy similar to the centrally planned exporting country. It adds that the similarity between the substitute and the exporting country will be reasonably defined, so that normal value in the exporting country, in the absence of a planned economy, can be approximated on the basis of the domestic price in the substitute country , considering economic criteria. 60. In accordance with the information and evidence presented by Vasconia in the present proceedings, the Secretariat noted that Brazil was a producer of aluminium pressure cookers. China and Brazil have similar production processes, they also have an availability of the main supplies for the manufacture of the product under investigation, including aluminum and bauxite. In addition, Brazil produced 801,700 tonnes of aluminum in 2017. Brazil is one of the world's leading electricity producers and has a large workforce. 61. As regards macroeconomic indicators, both countries are classified by the \uc2 World Economic Forum\uc2  as economies with a similar development index. 62. Based on the analysis described in the previous points of this Resolution and in accordance with Articles 33 of the LCE and 48 of the RLCE, the Secretariat reiterated its determination to consider Brazil's selection as a market economy country with a substitute China for normal value calculation purposes. d. Domestic prices in Brazil 63. The Applicant submitted aluminium pressure cooker pricing information to the Brazilian market. The information corresponded to retail quotes for that product that it obtained from the main self-service stores in that country. Among the Internet sites he consulted are \uc2 Walmart\uc2 , Ricardo Electro, Submarino, Casa Bahia, \uc2 Lojas Americanas\uc2 , Magazin Luiza, Lojas Colombo, Casa & Video, among others. It stated that this information came from public portals, and was the best information that it reasonably had available to it. 64. In order to support the conclusion that the products are manufactured in Brazil, it presented the profile of the manufacturers and a list of brands of aluminium pressure cookers manufactured by those companies. He also corroborated that the material of the products was aluminum in each quote and calculated a price per kilogram for aluminum pressure cookers. This is because it had specific weight-per-piece information in most quotes. 65. For price references where the pots were not weighed, a weight was assigned according to the following criteria: a. assigned the weight reported in other quotations of the same product (same brand, capacity and model); b. For pots of the same brand and capacity, the average weight of those who did (same brand and capacity) was applied, and c.\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0for products that only reported capacity, he applied the average weight of the pots that did report the weight, as long as, they were of the same capacity. 66. Because there were quotes outside the period investigated, the Applicant applied an inflation adjustment to bring them to that period and used the monthly inflation rate it obtained from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://es.inflation.eu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://es.inflation.eu}}}\uc2  website. It also applied the average exchange rate of real steer to dollars it obtained from the website {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mx.investing.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://mx.investing.com}}}\uc2 . 67. The Secretariat, for its part, revised the quotes provided by the Applicant, to identify characteristics such as trademarks, capacity, weight, date of issuance of the listing andmaterial from the product. On the other hand, it also identified quotes without information from the date of consultation and the product material, so it determined to exclude them from the calculation because it could not be ascertained that they corresponded to the period investigated and were elaborate pressure cookers aluminum. 68. At this stage of the investigation and on the basis of the availability of information, the Secretariat carried out the normal value calculation for the different aluminium pressure cookers identified in the export price according to the different capacities (4.5, 5 , 6, 7, 8 and 9 liters). However, in the case of aluminium pots with a capacity of 5, 8 and 9 litres, the Secretariat used the average price of the previous category available, because it did not have a comparable price in Brazil or the limited information available presents a bias in the pre- Cio. In the next stage of the investigation, the Secretariat would seek to arrive at greater elements on the prices of pots with a capacity of 5, 8 and 9 liters in the Brazilian market. 69. In accordance with Articles 2.1 of the AD Agreement, 3.1 of the LCE and 39 of the RLCE, the Secretariat calculated an average dollar price per kilogram for six categories of the investigated product. i. Adjustments to normal value 70. The Applicant proposed to adjust the normal value by terms and conditions of sale, specifically by the concepts of tax burdens, social contributions and margin of marketing. (1). Tax charges 71. Vasconia considered adjusting for the Tax on the Circulation of Goods and Services, of which it noted that tax rates range from 7% to 25% in accordance with Brazil's Supplementary Law 102 of 2000, however, considered 18% for this adjustment as stipulated in PFK Worldwide International Limited 2016/17, it noted that value-added taxes are not cumulative, so it is directly off-accounted for the price paid by the distributor. 72. In the case of the Industrialized Goods Tax (IPI), it considered a rate of 10% since aluminium pressure cookers have such a tax rate. To support its adjustment, it presented pFK Worldwide International Limited 2016/17 and the IPI table for 2017. It concluded that the tax is applied to the transaction price, so it is debited directly from the retail price. (2). Social contributions 73. In this case, Vasconia considered two contributions, specifically the Funding and Social Security Contribution (COFINS) and the Social Integration Program (PIS). It submitted a copy of Brazil's Law 9.718 for COFINS and Supplementary Law 123 for PIS, in addition to document PFK Worldwide International Limited 2016/17. They stipulate the corresponding tax rates ranging from 3% to 7.6% and 0.65% to 1.65%. Respectively. (3). Margin of marketing 74. Because the price references provided for calculating normal value are for trading companies, Vasconia proposed to deduct an amount per margin of market. To do this, it considered the financial statements for 2017 of the companies marketing aluminum pressure cookers listed on the Sao Paulo Stock Exchange, among which are: \uc2 Magazine Luiza\uc2 , Lonjas Americanas, B2W or Shoptime, Grupo Compa\u241\'00\'F1\u237\'00\'EDa Brazilian Distribution, Combo Market, \uc2 Wal-Mart\uc2  and Carrefour. Provided the financial statements of those marketers that you used to calculate the adjustment. 75. The Secretariat reviewed the statements of results referred to in the previous point and corroborated Vasconia's estimate of the margin of marketing, however, excluding From the estimated calculation for adjustment the financial information corresponding to \uc2 Walmart\uc2 , considering that this issales globally and not specific sales in the Brazilian market. It also ruled out Carrefour's financial information because, although it reported specific sales information in the Brazilian market, it did not specify the specific cost of sales in Brazil, but the total cost of sales globally. 76. In accordance with Articles 2.4 of the Anti-Dumping Agreement, 36 of the LCE and 53, 54 and 57 of the RLCE, the Secretariat determined to adjust the normal value by the concepts of tax burdens, social contributions and margin of marketing. 3. Price discrimination margin 77. In accordance with Articles 2.1, 6.8, and paragraphs 1 and 7 of Annex II of the AD Agreement, 30, 54 last paragraph and 64 of the LCE, and 38 and 39 of the RLCE, the Secretariat compared the normal value with the export price , and determined that imports of aluminium pressure cookers originating in China were made with a price discrimination margin of 135.75%. F. Damage and causation analysis 78. At this stage of the proceeding, no interested parties presented arguments and evidence contesting the determinations of the Resolution of Initiation. Therefore, the Secretariat conducted the analysis based on the arguments and evidence that Vasconia provided, in addition to the information that was reached at this stage of the investigation, in order to determine whether imports of aluminum pressure cookers originating in China , carried out under conditions of price discrimination, caused material injury to the domestic industry of the like product. 79. The analysis includes, inter alia, an examination of: (i) the volume of imports under conditions of price discrimination, their price and their effect on domestic prices of the like domestic product, and (ii) the impact of the volume and price of these imports into the economic and financial indicators of the domestic industry of the like product. 80. The analysis of the domestic industry's economic and financial indicators corresponds to the information that Vasconia provided, as it accounts for 100% of the domestic production of aluminium pressure cookers similar to those subject to as determined in point 122 of the Initiation Resolution and confirmed in point 106 of this Resolution. For this purpose, the Secretariat considered for its analysis data for the periods May 2015-April 2016, May 2016-April 2017 and May 2017-April 2018, which constitute the period analyzed and include the period investigated. Unless otherwise indicated, the behaviour of economic and financial indicators in a given year or period is analysed with respect to the comparable previous immediate. 1. Product similarity 81. In accordance with Articles 2.6 of the AD Agreement and 37 ft. II of the RLCE, the Secretariat assessed the information and evidence on the administrative record to determine whether domestically manufactured aluminum pressure cookers are similar to the product under investigation. 82. Vasconia stated that domestically manufactured aluminium pressure cookers are similar to the product under investigation, as there are no major differences affecting the similarity or degree of commercial interchangeability between the two products, in addition to having the same uses and functions; are made with the same supplies, through similar manufacturing processes, and comply with the same official Mexican standard. From a commercial point of view, both products supply the entire Mexican population, are marketed through wholesale distributors and marketers, reach the same consumers and are marketed in department stores and outlets Similar. To.Features 83. Vasconia noted that aluminium pressure cookers originating in China and domestically produced are goods that have similar physical characteristics and chemical composition, as the essential physical characteristics that identify the product object of research and the like product are the aluminum material of the body and cap, and consists of four main parts: (i) body or base with capacity up to 9 liters; ii) lid adjustable to pot body; (iii) pressure regulator and safety valve, and iv) handles and handles. They may include other components such as pressure indicator and other safety devices. 84. It indicated that the capacity of the product under investigation ranges from 2 to 9 liters and withstands a pressure of between 50 and 90 kilopascales, while the capacity of the like product ranged from 5 to 8 liters and withstands a pressure of between 80 and 115 kilopascales. 85. With regard to chemical composition, the Applicant noted that the body or base of the product under investigation and the like product is alloyed aluminium, the rest of the components may be plastic or Bakelite (handles and packaging) and steel (screws and valves). 86. Vasconia stated that the differences between the product under investigation and the domestically produced product are minimal and these differences are recorded in non-essential aspects such as colour, glossy or matte finish, handle design, etc. As for the physical characteristics, both products are similar and their uses are the same. 87. To support his assertions, Vasconia presented comparative tables with information on the physical characteristics and chemical composition of aluminium pressure cookers of Chinese origin and domestically produced, based on photographs, information from various websites of Chinese producers appearing as exporters to Mexico at the sat base, and the pressure cooker quality study, published in Consumer Review No. 51 of the Federal Consumer Attorney's Office (the "PROFECO study" ). As well as, data sheets of similar products of domestic manufacture withphotographs, technical descriptions, physics, components and capacity of the product. 88. In this regard, the Secretariat reviewed PROFECO's study and noted the following: a. Twenty-one models of twelve brands of domestic pressure cookers, made of aluminium and stainless steel, were analysed on the domestic market, considering models with capacities of around 6 litres. Each sample was tested thirteen in order to test its safety and efficiency; b. of the twenty-one models analyzed, seven were aluminum pressure cookers, four of which were produced in Mexico and three in China, and c.\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0results were presented for the following items: nominal working pressure, packaging and pot finishes, watertightness, hydrostatic pressure, hydrostatic body-cap separation test, combustion of handles and handles, heating speed, safety coefficient, packaging manufacturing material, characteristics, dimensions, heat sources on which you can work and number of safety systems. 89. Based on the information in the administrative file, the Secretariat had sufficient evidence to confirm that no significant differences were observed that discredited the physical and chemical characteristics of the pots of domestically produced aluminium pressure and those originating in China are similar, regardless of whether they have minor variations in their characteristics, a situation that does not compromise product similarity, as it allows them to comply with the same uses and functions and be commercially interchangeable,terms of the provisions of the legislation of the matter. Accordingly, the Secretariat preliminaryly determined that domestically produced and Chinese-produced aluminum pressure cookers have similar physical characteristics and chemical compositions. b. Production process 90. On the basis of information provided by Vasconia, the Secretariat found that aluminium pressure cookers, both native to China and domestically manufactured, are produced from the same inputs and similar production processes, which do not show substantial differences. As described in point 10 of this Resolution, the production of aluminum pressure cookers uses as main inputs the aluminium discs for the body and lid of the pot, components (plastic or Bakelite handles and handles , safety valve, pressure regulator, packaging) and electricity. In addition, its production process mainly includes the following stages: preparation of the aluminum disc, reception and inspection of raw materials, base die-cutting of the pot, grinding and washing, die-cutting of the pot lid, polishing and polishing of body and lid of the pot, assembly and packaging. 91. In order to prove the production process of Vasconia aluminum pressure cookers, it provided the following information: a. diagrams of the manufacturing process of aluminium pressure cookers of Chinese and domestic ally, as well as a comparative table of these production processes; b. the website {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.youtube.com}}}\uc2 , where a video showing the process of molding the base of an aluminum pressure cooker in China is seen; c. a video of the production process of manufacturing Vasconia's aluminum pressure cooker, and d.\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0the document Manufacturing of pressure cooker, which describes the production process of an aluminum pressure cooker, obtained from the website {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://es.slideshare.net"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://es.slideshare.net}}}\uc2 , on October 17, 2017. 92. On the basis of the information in the administrative file, the Secretariat determined that the product under investigation and the like domestic product generally have similar production processes, as they consist of the same stages and use similar imupmos. c. Standards 93. Based on the information on the administrative record, the Secretariat noted that domestically manufactured and Chinese-native aluminum pressure cookers comply with the Official Mexican Standard NOM-054-SCFI-1998, Household Utensils-Pots to pressure-Security. d. Uses and functions 94. As described in point 12 of this Resolution, the information available in the administrative file indicates that aluminium pressure cookers originating in China, as well as domestically manufactured ones, are primarily used for the rapid cooking of food by pressure inside, usually for domestic use. The above was corroborated with data sheets, Internet pages of Vasconia and some Chinese producers appearing as exporters to Mexico in the import database of SIC-M. As well as, with the study of PROFECO. e. Consumers and distribution channels 95. Vasconia stated that the aluminum pressure cookers imported from China and those of domestic manufacturing supply the same consumers: wholesale distributors and marketers. In addition, as a final product it reaches the same consumers and they are marketed in department stores and similar outlets. 96. It added that the product under investigation and the domestically manufactured product served the same geographic markets, that is, all the States of the Mexican Republic, mainly the most important cities in the country. 97. Vasconia with theto demonstrate that the product under investigation and the domestically manufactured product are marketed in the same marketing channels in Mexico, presented the PROFECO study. It stated that the study found the characteristics of Chinese and domestic aluminium pressure cookers marketed on the domestic market. 98. In this regard, the Secretariat revised PROFECO's study, as referred to in point 88 of this Resolution, and noted that twenty-one models of twelve brands of domestic pressure cookers, made of aluminium and stainless steel, were analyzed , which are marketed on the domestic market, considering models with capacities of around 6 litres. 99. The Secretariat therefore confirmed vasconia's presentation that: (i) the sample of the PROFECO study contains aluminium pressure pots with a capacity of about 6 litres, produced domestically and imported of Chinese origin; (ii) the information is addressed to the general public who are interested in acquiring a pressure cooker, and (iii) the aluminium pressure cookers were marketed on the domestic market. 100. In accordance with the arguments and evidence described above, the Secretariat preliminaryly determined that aluminium pressure cookers originating in China and domestically produced ones have the same consumers, are in the same markets and they serve the same distribution channels. f. Determination 101. Based on the results described in the previous points of this Resolution and the information available in the administrative file, the Secretariat preliminaryly determined that domestically manufactured aluminum pressure cookers are similar to those of the product under investigation, in terms of Articles 2.6 of the AD Agreement and 37 fraction II of the RLCE, since they have similar physical characteristics and composition, they are manufactured with the same inputs and through similar production processes that do not show substantial differences and cater to the same markets and consumers, allowing them to perform the same functions and be commercially interchangeable, so that they can be considered similar. 2. Domestic industry and representativeness 102. In accordance with Articles 4.1 and 5.4 of the AD Agreement, 40 and 50 of the LCE and 60, 61 and 62 of the RLCE, the Secretariat identified the domestic industry of the like product as the set of producers of aluminum pressure cookers , whose aggregate production constitutes all of the total domestic production of that product, taking into account whether the manufacturers are importers of the product under investigation or if there are elements indicating that they are linked to importing or exporting companies. 103. Vasconia stated that it is the only national producer of aluminium pressure cookers. To support it, he submitted a Letter from the Aluminium Institute A.C. of July 24, 2018. 104. It added that it did not import the product under investigation during the period under investigation or the product under investigation and that it was not linked to exporters or importers of the product under investigation. 105. In this regard, the Secretariat revised the basis of import statistics reported by the official list of import \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the SIC-M carried out through tariff fraction 7615.10.01 of the TIGIE, and also requested a number of actors representative sample of import pediments and their accompanying documentation, as referred to in point 123 of this Resolution. From the analysis of this information, vases' imports for the indicated fraction correspond to merchandiseunlike the product under investigation, vasconia therefore did not import the investigated product in the period analyzed. 106. The information available in the administrative file confirms that Vasconia constitutes the domestic industry by covering all producers of aluminium pressure cookers, in accordance with Articles 4.1 and 5.4 of the Agreement Anti-dumping, 40 and 50 of the LCE and 60, 61 and 62 of the RLCE, since it produced 100% of the total domestic production of the like product. In addition, no evidence is on the administrative record indicating that Vasconia is linked to exporters or importers of the product under investigation, or that it has made imports of aluminium pressure cookers originating in china. 3. International Market 107. Vasconia stated that it did not have at its fingertips specific information related to aluminum pressure cookers, so it submitted information from \uc2 the International Trade Centre\uc2  (ITC) on exports and imports under HS subheading 7615.10 for 2015, 2016 and 2017, classifying domestic aluminium articles and their parts; considered that the main exporting countries are the main producing countries and that the main importing countries are the main consuming countries. 108. Vasconia noted that China is well above the second exporting country, reaching a share of the total export volume of 61.49% in 2017, followed by Italy which participated with 5.86%, France with 4.03% and, fourthly, Turkey with 3.49%. Although these four countries showed export growth during 2017, China grew the fastest, achieving growth of 10.5%. 109. It also noted that the main importing countries in 2017 were: the United States that ranks first in imports of aluminium pressure cookers with 23.47% of total imports, followed by Japan (5.44%), Germany (5.25%), Belgium (3.98%), %) France (3.06%). The volume of the top five importing countries accounts for more than 40% of total imports. With respect to the trade balance, it had a deficit of 42,766 tonnes in 2017. 110. For the analysis of the international market, at this stage of the investigation, the Secretariat updated the figures obtained from the UN Comtrade statistics on world exports and imports under HS subheading 7615.10, for the period 2015 to 2017, since it considered that they correspond to the most restricted product range containing aluminum pressure cookers. Data show that world exports recorded an average annual increase of 3%, from 721.5 to 765.5 thousand tonnes from 2015 to 2017. In this regard, the Secretariat confirmed that in 2017 China was the world's largest exporter, during which period it concentrated 61.3% of the total, followed by Italy(5.8%), France (4.0%), Slovenia (3.7%) Turkey (3.5%).Exports by country of origin to the world through subheading 7615.10PositionCountryVolume in kilogramsI'm leaving. 2017(%)2015201620171china408,217,884424,884,603469,393,01161.3%2Italy40,396,99942,283,87144,742,6135.8%3France26,149,58228,442,36730,751,9604.0%4Slovenia427,453281,70228,531,3253.7%5Turkey20,802,35222,418,88526,602,8223.5%33Mexico1,331,8531,419,1491,490,9780.2%Rest of the World224,159,429199,048,747164,020,91321.4%Total General721,485,552718,779,324765,533,622100%Source: UN Comtrade. 111. Imports, meanwhile, saw an average annual decline of 0.4%, from 680.8 to 674.8 thousand tonnes from 2015 to 2017. In 2017, the top importers were the United States 23.9%, Japan 6.5%, Germany 5.8%, Belgium 4.6% and Slovenia 3.9%, whose imports accounted for 44.7% of totals. China and Mexico participated with 0.9% and 2% of total imports, respectively.\par \par \uc2 Imports by country of origin to the world through subheading 7615.10PositionCountryVolume in kilogramsI'm leaving. 2017 (%)2015201620171United States153,297,387175,271,904161,350,14523.9%2Japan49,559,95146,716,10443,776,9466.5%3Germany33,024,86633,625,60139,104,4635.8%4Belgium9,479,65112,703,28831,269,6694.6%5Slovenia770,546670,21326,108,1113.9%13Mexico12,872,5018,156,56913,723,0692.0%19china4,661,8616,622,9346,210,4460.9%Rest of the World417,117,428387,190,974353,291,64452.4%Total General680,784,191670,957,587674,834,493100%Source: UN Comtrade. 4. National Market 112. The information in the administrative file indicates that Vasconia is the only national producer of aluminium pressure cookers; while the main consumers are wholesale distributors and marketers. 113. Vasconia stated that the market demand performance for aluminium pressure cookers had no negative effect on the domestic industry, as Apparent National Consumption (ANC) has been increasing, and clearly the displacement of the aluminium pressure industry domestic production has been the result of the growth of the participation of the product under investigation in the Mexican market. 114. In this context of the placing on the market of aluminium pressure cookers, based on the economic indicators of the domestic industry and the import figures for SIC-M, adjusted as indicated in points 124 and 125 of this Resolution , the Secretariat noted that the domestic market for aluminium pressure cookers, as measured through the ANC (calculated as domestic production plus imports, less exports), showed mixed behaviour during the period analyzed, grew 7% in the period May 2016-April 2017 and decreased2% in the period investigated, so it accumulated a growth of 4% in the period analyzed. The performance of each ANC component was as follows: a. total imports increased by 28% in the may 2016-April 2017 period and decreased 11% and the period investigated, which meant cumulative growth of 14% in the period analyzed; b. emphasizes that during the period analysed, aluminium pressure cookers were imported from nine countries; in particular, in the period investigated the main suppliers were China, Hong Kong, Brazil, Germany and France, countries that accounted for 98%, 1.2%, 0.7%, 0.2% and 0.1% of the total imported volume, respectively; c. domestic production remained virtually unchanged by growing by only 0.1% in the period analyzed; increased 0.7% in the May 2016-April 2017 period and decreased 0.6% in the period investigated, and d.\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0total exports increased by 93% in the period analyzed, increasing by 27% in the may 2016-April 2017 period and decreasing 94% in the period investigated. 115. For its part, Domestic Market-Oriented Production (PNOMI), calculated as domestic production, minus exports, increased 0.4% in the period May 2016-April 2017 and 0.6% in the period investigated, so it cumulatively recorded 1% growth in the period analyzed. 5. Import analysis 116. In accordance with Articles 3.1 and 3.2 of the AD Agreement, 41 fraction I of the LCE and 64 fraction I of the RLCE, the Secretariat assessed the behaviour and trend of imports of the product under investigation during the period analysed, both in absolute terms and in relation to domestic production or consumption. 117. Vasconia stated that the increase in imports of Chinese-sourced aluminium pressure cookers in increasingly high quantities in the Mexican market is explained by the conditions under which they are made, such as the dumping price of the product imported price that is significantly lower than the prices of the like product in Mexico. 118. Indicated that total imports into Mexico of aluminium pressure cookers recorded increases of 70% during the period analyzed, while for the period investigated growth was 22% compared to its comparable period of the previous year. In this behavior, the volume imported originating in China, which accounted for 98% of the total imports of aluminium pressure cookers that Mexico acquires from abroad during the period investigated, was decisive. Even in the period before the investigated period, China accounted for 100% of total imports and this was due to significant sales at prices below production costs, a fact that prevented any other third-party supplier from offer their products in Mexico. 119. It noted that there was a significant increase in the volume of imports under conditions of price discrimination both in absolute terms and in relation to the ANC. Imports of Chinese-origin aluminum pressure cookers entering Mexico showed a 66% increase in the period analyzed, while in the investigated growth was 19%. 120. The Applicant provided the SAT import database for tariff fraction 7615.10.01 of the TIGIE, for the period from May 2015-April 2018, to obtain the value and volume of imports of pressure cookers Aluminum. 121. Vasconia stated that, in addition to the product under investigation, by tariff fraction 7615.10.01 of THE TIGIE, products other than the product investigated enter, so that in order to identify imports of the product under investigation,Vasconia excluded import \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  with descriptions of poorly classified product that must be entered for another tariff fraction, as well as pressure cookers with capacities greater than 9 litres, pans, mini pan sets, aluminum container sets for laboratory tests, aluminum caps, aluminum kitchen pot for popcorn and steel pressure cookers, electric, programmable, for cooking rice and for polymerization of dental sections. It identified the capacity of aluminium pressure cookers in order to exclude those with capacity greater than 9 litres. In cases where the product description did not report the capacity of aluminium pressure cookers, it identified such a characteristic on the basis of the criteria set out in point 27 of this Resolution. 122. As stated in point 29 of this Resolution and in order to estimate the value and volume of imports of aluminium pressure cookers, the Secretariat drew up the official list of import \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the SIC-M , corresponding to imports made through tariff fraction 7615.10.01 of the TIGIE, for the period analyzed. 123. Also, at this stage of the investigation, the Secretariat, in order to have more accurate information on the value and volume of imports corresponding to aluminium pressure cookers, was credited with a representative sample of pediments and invoices contributed by customs agents of tariff fraction 7615.10.01 of THE TIGIE, which accounted for 52% in the period May 2015-April 2016, 58% in May 2016-April 2017 and 100% in the period investigated, of the total volume imported of Chinese origin. 124. With the information identified in the previous point, the Secretariat reviewed the information available at this stage of the investigation for 48%, 49% and 73% of the total imported volume of Chinese origin for the May 2015-April periods of 2016, May 2016-April 2017 and the period investigated, respectively. However, at the next stage of the procedure, the rest of the information provided by customs agents will be reviewed. 125. The Secretariat incorporated the information referred to in the previous item and adjusted it with the \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the SIC-M, added the volumes and values, and on that basis carried out the import analysis and calculated the related indicators. 126. In accordance with the import statistics identified in the previous two points of this Resolution, the Secretariat noted that total imports recorded an increase of 14% over the period analyzed; in the period May 2016-April 2017 they increased 28% and in the period investigated they decreased 11%. This behavior is largely explained by the performance of imports of the product under investigation. 127. Indeed, imports originating in China increased 12% during the period analyzed; 28% growth in the may 2016-April 2017 period and decreased by 13% in the period investigated, and contributed almost 100% of total imports in the May 2015-April 2016 and May 2016-April 2017 periods , while in the period investigated the contribution was 98%, which meant a decrease of 2 percentage points in the period analyzed. 128. For its part, imports of the other origins, since they were not in absolute terms significant, it is apparent that their share of total imports over the period analyzed increased from 0.004% in the period May 2015-April 2016 to 2.2% in the period investigated; 2.16 percentage points in the period analyzed. It should be noted that in the period May 2016-April 2017 there were no imports oforigins other than China. Imports of aluminum pressure cookers Source: SIC-M. 129. In terms of the domestic market, the Secretariat noted that total imports increased their share of the ANC by 4.6 percentage points in the period May 2016-April 2017 and decreased by 2.3 percentage points in the period investigated, going from 22.9% to 25.1% (27.4% in the may 2016-April 2017 period). The performance of total imports in the ANC is primarily explained by the share of imports originating in China. 130. In fact, the investigated imports accounted for 22.9% of the ANC in the May 2015-April 2016 period, 27.4% in the may 2016-April 2017 period and 24.5% in the period investigated, increasing their share of the domestic market by 1.7 points percentage points in the period analyzed. In relation to the total volume of domestic production, the investigated imports accounted for 29.3%, 37.3% and 32.7% in the periods May 2015-April 2016, May 2016-April 2017 and in the period investigated, respectively, which meant 3.4 percentage points increase over the period analyzed. 131. As regards imports from other sources, they increased their participation in the ANC by 0.5 percentage points in the period analysed, from 0.001% in the period May 2015-April 2016 to 0.5% in the period investigated. Percentage Structure of the ANC Source: Information provided by the Applicant and SIC-M. 132. In addition, the pNOMI of the domestic industry decreased its participation in the ANC by 2.2 percentage points in the period analyzed, from 77.1% in the period May 2015-April 2016 to 74.9% in the period investigated (72.6% in the May 2016-April period of 2 017), virtually attributable to imports under conditions of price discrimination. 133. The results described in the previous points of this Resolution allow the Secretariat to determine in the near hand that the investigated imports were increasingly trending in absolute terms and in relation to the ANC and production during the period under review, while the domestic industry declined its market share, attributable to the increase in imports originating in China that were made under conditions of price discrimination. In this sense, the growth of the domestic market did not result in a benefit to the domestic industry, whereby imports of the investigated merchandise and their share were increased, while PNOMI decreased its share of the market in the period analyzed. 134. According to the information in the administrative file, the Secretariat confirmed that the ANC of aluminium pressure cookers recorded growth of 4% during the period analysed. However, the growth of the ANC in the period analyzed is lower than the growth recorded in the volume of investigated imports of 12%. 6. Price effects 135. In accordance with Articles 3.1 and 3.2 of the AD Agreement, 41 ft II of the LCE and 64(II) of the RLCE, the Secretariat analysed whether the investigated imports entered the Mexican market at prices considerably lower than those of the domestic product, or whether the effect of such imports was to depress domestic prices or to prevent the otherwise occurring increase; and whether the level of import prices was decisive in explaining their behaviour in the domestic market. 136. Vasconia statedthat the price effects of aluminum pressure cookers are the result of high dumping margins with which Chinese-origin aluminum pressure cookers are exported and these low prices, in turn, are the result of the distortions caused by the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the Chinese government in the aluminium market and its products, which is reflected in the distorted prices of the product under investigation in both international markets and Mexico. 137. It noted that under China's export dumping practices to Mexico, prices for Chinese aluminum pressure cookers were well below the prices of domestic aluminum pressure cookers, an explaining that imports have increased their share of the domestic market as they have in the world. 138. It noted that although there were slight increases in the prices of aluminium pressure cookers of Chinese origin in the period investigated, they were explained by global trends, which did not reverse the price distortion of the Chinese product, which continues to be below the cost of production of Vasconia. 139. In assessing the Applicant's arguments, the Secretariat calculated the average implicit prices of subject imports and other countries, based on the values and volumes obtained as described in points 124 and 125 of the this Resolution, and noted that the average price of imports from other sources accumulated a decrease of 37% in the period under review, reiterating that no imports from other sources were imported from other sources during the May 2016-April 2017 period. Meanwhile, the average price of investigated imports increased by 4% in the may 2016-April 2017 period, 25% in the may 2017-April 2018 period, accumulating a 30% increase in the period analyzed. 140. As regards the average price of sales to the domestic market of the domestic industry (measured in dollars), it decreased 9% in the period May 2016-April 2017 and increased 11% in the period investigated, which meant cumulative growth of 1% in the period Analyzed. 141. In assessing the existence of undervaluation, the Secretariat compared the plant FOB price of sales to the domestic industry's domestic market with the price of the investigated imports; to do so, the latter price was adjusted with customs agent fees, customs processing duties and the corresponding tariff. 142. While it is true that the prices of both investigated imports and domestic industry prices increased in the period investigated, the Secretariat noted that the average price of investigated imports, made in conditions of price discrimination, was below the national price at 44% in the period May 2015-April 2016, 36% in the period May 2016-April 2017 and 27% in the period investigated. Import and domestic product prices Source: Information provided by the Applicant and SIC-M. 143. Relative to the average price of imports from other origins, the price of aluminium pressure cookers originating in China was considerably lower in the May 2015-April 2016 periods and the period investigated, in percentages of 58% and 21% , respectively, considering that no imports from other origins were registered in the May 2016-April 2017 period. 144. In accordance with the results described in the previous points of this Resolution, the Secretariat preliminaryly determined that during the period under investigation the subject imports were made withsignificant levels of undervaluation with respect to national price and other sources of supply, which are associated with the practice of price discrimination they incurred, the margin of which was set out in point 77 of this Resolution. Undervaluation incentivized demand for imports of Chinese origin, as well as increased domestic market share in the period under review, to the detriment of the domestic aluminum pressure cooker industry. 7. Effects on the domestic industry 145. Based on Articles 3.1 and 3.4 of the AD Agreement, 41 fraction III of the LCE and 64 fraction III of the RLCE, the Secretariat assessed the effects of imports of aluminium pressure cookers originating in China on indicators economic and financial industries of the domestic industry of the like product. 146. Vasconia stated that the impact of the domestic industry is due to the investigated imports; that while consumption grew in the period analyzed and the domestic industry was displaced from the Mexican market, imports of Chinese-origin aluminum pressure cookers gained a significant market share. 147. He noted that only the distortions caused by China's unfair practices in the Mexican market explain that in a period of constant growth in demand for aluminum pressure cookers, Vasconia has such negative and erratic behaviors in its production, sales and prices in the market. China even prevents Vasconia from improving its sales, prices, underutilization of installed capacity and employment. 148. In order to assess Vasconia's arguments, the Secretariat considered the data of its economic and financial indicators corresponding to the like product, since Vasconia was the one that makes up the domestic industry, except for those factors that accounting reasons it is not feasible to identify with the same level of specificity (cash flow, capital raising capacity, return on investment and the contribution of the like product in the latter indicator) their financial statements were used internal or internal fiscal years 2015 to 2017 and January-April 2017 and 2018. The cost, sales and profits statements for domestic, export and total goods for 2015, 2016 and 2017 and the May 2015-April 2016, May 2016-April 2017 and May 2017-April 2018, were also analyzed. In order to make the financial figures comparable to each other, the financial information was updated using the method of changes in the overall price level using the National Consumer Price Index published by the National Institute of Statistics and Geography. 149. The information that Vasconia provided indicated that in the light of the mixed market performance, the Secretariat noted that the domestic industry's production of aluminium pressure cookers practically maintained its level, registering a 0.1% increase in the period analyzed: increased 0.7% in the period May 2016-April 2017 and decreased 0.6% in the period investigated. 150. PNOMI of the domestic industry grew by 1% in the period analyzed, 0.4% in the period May 2016-April 2017 and 0.6% in the period investigated. 151. The Secretariat also noted that the market growth during the period under review benefited the most investigated imports, gaining market share, to the detriment of the domestic industry. The domestic industry's PNOMI lost 2.2 percentage points of participation in the ANC in the period analyzed (lost 4.6 and grew 2.3 percentage points in the May 2016-April period2017 and the period investigated, respectively). For its part, the investigated imports gained 4.6 in the period May 2015-April 2016 and lost 2.9 percentage points of participation in the period investigated, accumulating an increase in their share of 1.7 percentage points in the period while imports from other sources recorded a marginal increase of 0.5 percentage points in the period analyzed. 152. The results described in the previous point indicate that the market loss recorded by the domestic industry is linked to the increase in investigated imports, which were the mainly beneficiarie of the growth of the market during the period analyzed. 153. The performance of the total sales (to the domestic and external market) of the domestic industry increased by 5% in the period analyzed: they increased 16% in the period May 2016-April 2017 and decreased 9% in the period investigated. In this regard, the Secretariat noted that the performance of Vasconia's total sales is largely explained by the behaviour of its domestic sales: a. sales to the domestic market of the domestic industry increased 7% in the period analyzed; increased 16% in the may 2016-April 2017 period, and subsequently declined by 8% in the period investigated; while export sales decreased 93% in the period analyzed (increased 27% in the May 2016-April 2017 period and fell 94% in the period investigated), and b.\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0Vasconia's exports accounted for on average 0.8% of its production during the period analyzed, reflecting that the domestic industry is fundamentally dependent on the domestic market, where it competes with imports under conditions of price discrimination. 154. The Secretariat therefore considered that the decrease in domestic sales of the domestic industry in the period investigated is explained by the level of prices to which the investigated imports of the Mexican market occurred to the Mexican market during the period analysed, because they had lower prices than the like domestic product, as according to the results described in point 142 of this Resolution, they recorded significant undercutting margins of 44% in the period May 2015-April 2016, 36% in the next comparable period and 27% in the period investigated. 155. As regards the installed capacity of the domestic industry to produce aluminium pressure cookers remained unchanged in the period analysed. 156. As a result of the performance of installed capacity and production, the use of the first of these indicators remained almost constant during the period analysed; increased by 0.3 percentage points in the May 2016-April 2017 period from 40.3% to 40.6%, and decreased by 0.3 percentage points in the period investigated, reaching a utilization of 40.3%. 157. Vasconia argued that despite growth in demand, capacity utilization has remained at levels of 40%. The Secretariat considered this argument reasonable, taking into account the percentages of utilization recorded by the domestic industry, described in the previous point, and the growth recorded by the market during the period analyzed (4%), which benefited investigated imports, to the detriment of the domestic industry, by limiting the growth of its domestic sales, production and utilization of installed capacity in the period investigated. 158. The inventories of the domestic industry decreased by 37% in the period analyzed; 27% and 14% in the May 2016-April 2017 periods and the investigated period, respectively. 159. The Secretariatnoted that the average employment of the domestic industry decreased by 1% and 6% in the May 2016-April 2017 period and the period investigated, respectively, which meant a decrease of 7% in the period analyzed. 160. Production and employment performance resulted in the increase in the productivity of the domestic industry (measured as the ratio of these indicators) by 2% in the period May 2016-April 2017 and 6% in the period investigated (increased 8% in the period alizado). In the same periods, the salary associated with the production of aluminium pressure cookers decreased by 6% and 5%, respectively (down 11% in the period analyzed). 161. The Secretariat assessed the financial situation of the domestic industry on the basis of the cost, sales and profits of similar goods for the domestic, export and total markets for 2015, 2016 and 2017, and the periods May 2015-April 2016, May 2016-April 2017 and May 2017-April 2018. 162. In this regard, the Secretariat noted that the volume of sales in the export market was not significant, accounting on average at 1% of the total market volume sold during the period analyzed; which finds that the domestic industry is fundamentally dependent on the domestic market. Therefore, the Secretariat assessed the effects of investigated imports, under conditions of price discrimination, on Vasconia's financial indicators, considering sales to the domestic market. 163. Based on the information noted in the previous points of this Resolution, the Secretariat noted that the conduct of the volumes and prices of the domestic industry was reflected in the performance of its sales revenue to the market (measured in pesos) as follows: they increased 7.4% in 2016 and decreased 10.4% in 2017, a decrease of 3.8% during the period 2015 to 2017. 164. Operating costs resulting from sales to the domestic market (measured as the sum of sales costs plus operating expenses) increased 12.3% in 2016 and decreased 10.8% in 2017, so that in the period from 2015 to 2017 they grew by 0.2%. 165. The performance of operating revenues and costs was reflected in a decrease in operating profit of 48.9% during the period 2015 to 2017, resulting from a fall of 49.2% in 2016 and an increase 0.6% in 2017. 166. As a result of operating profit behavior, operating margin decreased by 4.2 percentage points from 8% in 2015 to 3.8% in 2016, then increased by 0.4 percentage points to 4.2% in 2017. 167. For its part, during the periods of the period analyzed, sales revenue to the domestic market (measured in pesos) behaved as follows: they increased 15.5% in the period May 2016-April 2017 and decreased 7% in the period an increase of 7.5% during the period analyzed. 168. Operating costs resulting from sales to the domestic market increased by 11.8% in the May 2016-April 2017 period and decreased by 5.5% in the period investigated, with 5.7% growing in the period analyzed. 169. The performance of operating income and costs was reflected in an increase in operating profit of 91.4% during the period analyzed, resulting from the increase of 194% in the period May 2016-April 2017 and a decrease of 34.9% in the period investigated. 170. As a result of the behaviour during the period analyzed as a whole of operating profits, operating margin increased by 3.1 percentage points from 2% in the May 2015-April 2016 period to 5.1% in the May 2016-April 2017 period , subsequently decreased by 1.5 percentage points3.6% in the period investigated. 171. With regard to Return of the Investment in Assets (ROA) variables, roa deal, ROA-like product contribution, cash flow and ability to raise capital, in accordance with the provisions of Articles 3.6 of the AD Agreement and 66 of the RLCE, the effects of the investigated imports were assessed from Vasconia's dictated or internal financial statements, which consider the production of the most restricted group or range of products including the similar product. 172. With respect to the ROA of the domestic industry (calculated at the \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  level) showed a mixed trend in the years that are part of the period analyzed, being 4.7%, 2.6% and 5.3% for 2015, 2016 and 2017, respectively. In the January-April 2017 and 2018 periods, it represented -0.2% and 1.7%, respectively. 173. The contribution of the like product to the Applicant's ROA (calculated at the \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  level) showed a downward trend in the years that are part of the period analyzed being 0.4% in 2015 and 0.2% in 2016 and 2017. In the January-April 2017 and 2018 periods, the contribution of the like product to the ROA represented -0.2% and 0.1%, respectively. 174. From Vasconia's cash flow statements, the Secretariat noted that cash flow at the \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  level reported positive performance in 2016 compared to 2015 by increasing by 137.5%, but decreased by 59.2% in 2017 compared to 2016; 3.2% decrease during the period 2015 to 2017. In the January-April 2018 period, compared to its comparable comparable period of 2017, operating cash flow decreased by 13.9%. 175. The Applicant's ability to raise capital was analyzed through the behaviour of the applicant's solvency, liquidity, leverage and debt indices. In this regard, Vasconia's solvency and liquidity levels retained acceptable levels from 2015 to 2017; in general, a ratio of current assets to short-term liabilities of 1 to 1 or higher is considered appropriate. The current ratio (ratio between current assets and short-term liabilities) for Vasconia was 2.81 in 2015, in the order of 2.45 in 2016 and 2.03 in 2017; while for the January-April 2017 and 2018 periods they were 2.95 and 3.15, respectively. The acid test (circulating asset minus the value of inventories, relative to short-term liabilities) or ratio of fast-performing assets, recorded levels of 1.52, 1.58 and 1.21 pesos for each weight of debt in the short term in 2015 , 2016 and 2017, respectively, while in the periods January-April 2017 and 2018 they were 1.61 and 1.66 pesos, respectively. 176. The leverage index has remained at acceptable levels in the period 2015 to 2017 (except in the January-April 2017 and 2018 periods). Typically, a proportion of total liabilities to book capital less than 100% is considered manageable, in this case Vasconia's leverage levels represented 97%, 95% and 96%, for 2015, 2016 and 2017, respectively. For their part, for the periods January-April 2017 and 2018 they accounted for 119% and 126%, respectively. 177. As regards the level of debt or total liability ratio for total assets, it remained at acceptable levels. Vasconia's debt level accounted for 49% in 2015, 2016 and 2017; while for the January-April 2017 and 2018 periods it accounted for 54% and 56%, respectively. 178. Based on the results described in the previous points of this Resolution, the Secretariat preliminarydetermined that the increase in investigated imports in both absolute and relative terms, under conditions of discrimination of prices and the low price levels at whichsignificant undervaluation margins during the period analyzed, caused an impact on relevant economic indicators of the domestic industry, in particular, in the period investigated there was a decrease in following indicators: production, internal market sales, wages and employment. In addition, it points out that the domestic industry recorded relatively low utilization levels of its installed capacity (40.3% in the period investigated, 40.6% in the period May 2016-April 2017 and 40.3% in the previous comparable period). 179. With regard to the operating results of domestic sales of the product similar to that investigated, the Secretariat saw a 48.9% decrease in operating profits during the years 2015 to 2017 that are part of the period analyzed. This decrease resulted from a 3.8% decline in sales revenue and a slight increase in operating costs of 0.2%, resulting in a decrease in operating margin of 3.8 percentage points from 8% in 2015 to a margin of 4.2% in 2017. In the period investigated, the following domestic industry financial variables associated with domestic sales were observed: sales revenue decreased by 7%, operating profits decreased by 34.9% and operating margin decreased by 1.5 percentage points. 8. Other damage factors 180. In accordance with Articles 3.5 of the AD Agreement, 39 last paragraph of the LCE and 69 of the RLCE, the Secretariat examined the concurrence of factors other than imports originating in China under conditions of price discrimination, than at the at the same time could be the cause of material injury to the domestic aluminium pressure cooker industry. 181. Vasconia stated that there are no factors other than imports under conditions of price discrimination that have caused injury to the domestic industry. In this regard, it argued that: a. Imports from other sources are not the cause of injury to domestic industry, since the volume of such imports is almost zero, and b. the market demand performance of aluminium pressure cookers did not have negative effects on the domestic industry, as the ANC has been increasing and clearly the displacement of the domestic industry has been due to the growth of the share of chinese-sourced aluminum pressure cooker in the market Mexican. 182. The Secretariat analysed the possible effects of import volumes and prices from other countries, the export performance of domestic industry and the behaviour of the domestic market during the period under review, as well as other factors that could relevant to explain the performance of the domestic industry. 183. According to the information in the administrative file, the Secretariat noted that the demand for the product under investigation, in terms of the ANC, recorded a cumulative growth of 4% in the period analyzed and in the period investigated decreased 2%. The CONtraction of the ANC during the period investigated is explained by the decrease in imports originating in China, which contributed 98% of total imports. However, it should be noted that in the face of the market growth of 4% during the period analyzed, the investigated imports increased their share of the ANC by 1.7 percentage points, while in the same period PNOMI decreased 2.2 percentage points, mainly attributable to the investigated imports, given the low prices at which they were made, as they achieved an undervaluation of between 27% and 44% compared todomestically manufactured product over the period analyzed. 184. In this context of market behavior, the Secretariat had no evidence to indicate that imports from other sources could cause injury to the domestic industry, since: a. in absolute terms, non-investigated imports were significant, given that their share of total imports over the period analyzed rose from 0.004% in the May 2015-April 2016 period to 2.2% in the period investigated; increasing by 2.16 percentage points in the period analyzed; It should be noted that in the period May 2016-April 2017 there were no imports from non-China origins; b. increased their participation in the ANC by just 0.5 percentage points in the period analyzed, from 0.001% in the period May 2015-April 2016 to 0.5% in the period investigated, and c.\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0the average price of imports from other sources was above the price of domestic sales to the domestic market 34% in the period May 2015-April 2016, while in the period investigated it was below 9%. In relation to the price of investigated imports, in the same periods it was higher at 140% and 26%, respectively. 185. As regards the export performance of the domestic industry, as indicated in point 114(d) of this Resolution, exports decreased 93% in the period analysed (increased by 27% in the period May 2016-April 2017 and down 94% in the period investigated); however, they accounted on average for 0.8% of production during the period analyzed, reflecting that the domestic industry is fundamentally dependent on the domestic market, where it competes with imports under conditions of discrimination prices, so that they did not contribute fundamentally to the performance of the economic and financial indicators of the domestic industry. 186. Furthermore, the Secretariat determined that productivity behaviour could not cause harm to the domestic industry, as this indicator accumulated growth of 8% during the period analyzed (increased 2% in the period May 2016-April 2017 and 6% period investigated). Furthermore, the information on the record does not indicate that technological innovations or changes in the consumption structure, or restrictive business practices that could affect the performance of the domestic industry, have occurred. 187. In accordance with the analysis in the previous points of this Resolution and the information in the administrative file, the Secretariat determined at the outset that it did not identify factors other than imports originating in China, under conditions of price discrimination, which at the same time could be the cause of material injury to the domestic industry. 9. Additional items 188. Based on itC export statistics under HS subheading 7615.10, Vasconia stated that China's exports are well above the second exporting country, reaching a 61.49% share in 2017. He noted that China is one of the countries with the highest growth in their exports, 10.5% in 2017. It presented a table showing that the prices at which China exports aluminium pressure cookers are the lowest globally and have steadily declined. 189. With respect to China's export profile, and as described in point 110 of this Resolution, the Secretariat updated the figures obtained from the UN Comtrade statistics on world exports under HS subheading 7615.10, and confirmed that China was the main exporter of aluminium pressure cooker, during theperiod from 2015 to 2017. During the same period, Chinese exports accounted for 59% of total exports of aluminium pressure cookers globally; and its exports increased by 15%, from 408.2 to 469.4 thousand tonnes. The latter volume is equivalent to more than 300 and 400 times the size of the ANC and the domestic production, respectively, of the period investigated. Mexico also remained at number 33, from 2015 to 2017, in terms of its importance as a destination for Chinese exports, with an average share of 1% of total exports. 190. At this stage of the investigation, and in response to the request made by the Secretariat, Vasconia presented production figures, installed capacity, domestic sales and inventories of flat-rolled products from China for 2015, reported in the study "Aluminum: Competitive Conditions Affecting the U.S. Industry", consulted on the website {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usitc.gov"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.usitc.gov}}}\uc2 , because it was the information that was reasonably available. It also submitted information on Chinese companies producing the product under investigation. 191. The Secretariat analysed the information identified in the previous point and noted that in 2015 China's installed capacity, production and sales of flat-rolled products is far superior to the production and ANC production and ANC of aluminium pressure cookers in the Mexican market during the period May 2015-April 2016. It also highlights that Chinese industry has a freely available capacity of 5,553 thousand tons. 192. Based on the results described in the previous points of this Resolution, the Secretariat preliminarydetermined that China has a significant export potential relative to the size of the Mexican market and domestic production, which which, in addition to the growth of investigated imports into the domestic market in absolute and relative terms, and their low price levels during the period analyzed, constitute sufficient elements underpinning the well-founded likelihood of china's imports continue to increase in the immediate future and aggravate injury to the domestic industry. G. Conclusions 193. Based on the comprehensive analysis of the arguments and evidence described in this Resolution, the Secretariat preliminaryly concluded that, during the period investigated, imports of aluminium pressure cookers originating in China were made in conditions of price discrimination and caused material injury to the domestic industry of the like product. Among the main elements assessed in a comprehensive manner, which support this conclusion, without being considered exhaustive or limiting, the following are: a. Imports of the product under investigation were made with a margin of 135.75% price discrimination. In the period investigated, imports originating in China accounted for 98% of total imports. b. Imports of aluminium pressure cookers originating in China increased in absolute and relative terms. In the period analyzed they recorded growth of 12% and increased their share in relation to the ANC by 1.7 percentage points, going from a contribution of 22.9% in the period May 2015-April 2016 to 24.5% in the period investigated. In relation to the volume of domestic production, they recorded an increase of 3.4 percentage points, from 29.3% in the period May 2015-April 2016 to 32.7% in the period investigated. c. During the period analyzed, the average price of imports of aluminium pressure cookers originating in China was below the domestic selling price of thedomestic industry (in percentages ranging from 27% to 44%), and the average price of imports from other sources (in percentages between 21% and 58%). d.\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0The low price of the investigated imports over the period under review is a determining factor incentivized their increase and share of the domestic market, to the detriment of the domestic industry. e. In the period investigated, the concurrence of the investigated imports adversely affected some relevant economic indicators of the domestic industry, including production, domestic sales, wages and employment. In addition, the domestic industry recorded relatively low levels of installed capacity utilization (40.3% in the period investigated and 40.6% in the previous comparable period). f. The operating performance of the domestic industry by domestic sales recorded a 48.9% decrease in operating profits during the years 2015 to 2017 that are part of the period analyzed; this decrease resulted from a 3.8% decline in sales revenue and a slight increase in operating costs of 0.2%, resulting in a decrease in operating margin of 3.8 percentage points from 8% in 2015 to a margin of 4.2% in 2017. In the period investigated, the following domestic industry financial variables associated with domestic sales were observed: sales revenue decreased by 7%, operating profits decreased by 34.9% and operating margin decreased by 1.5 percentage points. G.\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0No other injury factors than imports originating in China were identified. h. The available information indicates that China has a potential exporter that is several times the size of the domestic market for similar goods. H. Countervailing Fee 194. Due to the positive preliminary determination on price and injury discrimination to the domestic aluminium pressure cooker industry, and taking into account the vulnerability of the domestic industry to the concurrence of aluminium pressure cookers imports under conditions of price discrimination, the Secretariat determined appropriate to impose a provisional countervailing fee to prevent further injury to the domestic industry during the investigation, as Articles 7.1 and 9.1 of the ANTI-Dumping Agreement and 62 of the LCE. 195. On the basis of the information in the administrative file, the Secretariat considered it appropriate to apply a countervailing quota lower than the price discrimination margin, in an amount sufficient to restore fair conditions of competition and eliminate the injury caused to the domestic industry of the like merchandise. For this purpose, the Secretariat considered as a non-harmful price the average normal value proposed by Vasconia validated at this stage of the investigation for the calculation of the price discrimination margin, and compared it with the average price at which the investigated during the period investigated, to calculate the amount of the countervailing quota. 196. Thus, in accordance with Articles 9.1 of the AD Agreement and 62 second paragraph of the LCE, the Secretariat determined that a countervailing quota of 67.72% would allow the prices of investigated imports to be brought to the level of the non-harmful price to the domestic industry, which would be sufficient to correct the price distortion caused by investigated imports and eliminate injury to the domestic industry of the like merchandise. 197. For the above,Articles 7 and 9.1 of the AD Agreement and 57 fraction I and 62 second paragraph of the LCE, is appropriate to issue the following RESOLUTION 198. The investigation procedure in the field of unfair international trade practices, in its form of price discrimination, continues, and a provisional countervailing quota of 67.72% is imposed on imports of aluminium pressure cookers originating in China, regardless of the country of origin, entering by tariff fraction 7615.10.01 or any other. 199. On the basis of Article 87 of the LCE, the countervailing quota shall apply to the customs value declared in the corresponding order. 200. It is for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Public Credit to apply the countervailing quota throughout the national territory. 201. On the basis of Articles 7.2 of the AD Agreement and 65 of the LCE, interested parties may ensure payment of the corresponding provisional countervailing quota, in some of the forms provided for in the CFF. 202. In accordance with Article 66 of the LCE, importers who, under this Resolution, are required to pay the provisional countervailing fee, shall not be obliged to pay the provisional countervailing fee if they find that the country of origin of the goods is different from China. The verification of the origin of the good shall be carried out in accordance with the provisions of the Agreement laying down the rules for the determination of the country of origin of the imported goods and the provisions for their certification, for non-preferential purposes (previously Agreement laying down the rules for the determination of the country of origin of imported goods and the provisions for their certification, relating to countervailing quotas) published in the DOF on 30 August 1994, and their amendments published in the DOF on 30 August 1994, and their amendments published in 11 November 1996, 12 October 1998, 30 July 1999, 30 June 2000, 1 and 23 March 2001, 29 June 2001, 6 September 2002, 30 May 2003 , 14 July 2004, 19 May 2005, 17 July 2008 and 16 October 2008. 203. On the basis of the second paragraph of Article 164 of the RLCE, a period of 20 working days, from the publication of this Resolution in the DOF, is granted for interested parties accredited in the proceedings to consider it appropriate , compare to the Secretariat to present any additional arguments and evidence they deem relevant. This period will end at 14:00 on the day of its expiration. 204. The presentation of such arguments and evidence must be made to the official party of the UPCI, located in Insurgentes Sur 1940, ground floor (window area), Col. Florida, C.P. 01030, Mexico City. Such presentation must be made in original and three copies, plus the corresponding acknowledgement of receipt. 205. Please communicate this Resolution to the SAT for legal purposes. 206. Notify the interested parties of the interested parties of their knowledge. 207. This Resolution shall enter into force on the day following its publication in the DOF. Mexico City, as of June 17, 2019.- The Secretary of Economy, Graciela M\u225\'00\'E1rquez Col\u237\'00\'EDn.- Rubric.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020190626ef6q004sc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
