\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 , Trump's New Field of Trade War\b0\par\par\uc2 667 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juni 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 U.S. President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's renewed obsession with what he calls "unfair" exchange rates open the door to a new battle with potential to severely damage the global economy.\par \par \uc2 Trump has spent two years attacking the pillars of the global trading system and has not hesitated to wage tariff wars against various allies and adversaries.\par \par \uc2 And this confrontation may intensify from next month, when a rule that empowers Washington to impose punitive tariffs on any country that it believes handles its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to make its products more competitive will come into force. in front of the Americans.\par \par \uc2 The representative has frequently attacked eurozone countries such as Germany for benefiting from a relatively weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "They've been getting away with it for years with China and others," he said last week.\par \par \uc2 As Trump's attack on \uc2 Mario Draghi\uc2 , president of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , monetary policy movements that previously went unnoticed are now ammunition to justify the representative's retaliation.\par \par \uc2 Economists warn that this opens the door to a great global monetary war in which all are pitted against all.\par \par \uc2 If Trump continues down this path, probably with the support of his Commerce Secretary, \uc2 Wilbur Ross\uc2 , the United States would be vulnerable to retaliation from other countries if the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  cuts interest rates, just as the White House tenant has asked in Repeatedly.\par \par \uc2 Central banks cut interest rates to stimulate a depressed economy. The value of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is weakened in exchange for boosting exports, which then propel economic growth.\par \par \uc2 Mark Sobel, a former Treasury official under Republican and democratic administrations, claimed to have "serious reservations" about this White House plan.\par \par \uc2 In a plea to Commerce, it asserts that this rule is "fundamentally erroneous... and could backfire and damage the U.S. economy."\par \par \uc2 Doubtful legality\par \par \uc2 For years, lawmakers and presidents, both Democrats and Republicans, have launched plans to pursue governments that manipulate their kind of field to compete in global trade.\par \par \uc2 But these efforts, mainly focused on China, have faced strong resistance and have finally been abandoned, in part because they were seen as a way to violate the rules of global trade.\par \par \uc2 Ironically, \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets in recent years, except to prevent the yuan from falling. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has gained value since the financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  issues a report twice a year on possible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulations.\par \par \uc2 Since the mid-1990s, no country has been labelled as manipulative, not even China, despite its efforts to maintain a weak yuan.\par \par \uc2 Commerce has made moves to rob the Treasury of control over this matter with a legal amendment that would allow it to treat \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation in the same way it does with, for example, subsidies that foreign governments give to companies that hurt American ones.\par \par \uc2 If approved, the department could impose tariffs to offset the weakest exchange rate against the US dollar. Commerce has been open to public feedback on this change until June 27, and from that day you can implement it at any time.\par \par \uc2 According to the proposal, Commerce said it will accept the Treasury's assessment of whether a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is undervalued, "unless we have good reason to believe otherwise."\par \par \uc2 This ambiguity has ignitedalarms among economists, many of whom believe commerce does not have the technical expertise to make such an assessment.The plan would "grant excessive discretion to the Commerce Department," Sobel said.\par \par \uc2 It is notoriously difficult to objectively calculate whether a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is undervalued and, if so, how much it is.\par \par \uc2 For years, the \uc2 Peterson Institute for International Economics\uc2  issued a report assessing exchange rates, but stopped doing so "because they were completely arbitrary," the head of the expert group, \uc2 Adam Posen\uc2 , recently told the press.\par \par \uc2 "China should have been hit hard in the early 2000s by massive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation," Posen said, but doing so now is "pretty close to the absurd."\par \par \uc2 Copyright Group of Diarios Am\u233\'00\'E9rica - GDA/La Nacion/Costa Rica\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020190623ef6n0043l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
