ars to be having some effect. USD/CNY gapped down Monday, touching a low of 6.8854 from Friday's close of 6.9005, reacting to authorities' verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the weekend. The \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  Banking and Insurance Regulatory Commission (CBIRC) on Saturday said "those who speculate and short the yuan will for sure suffer heavy loss". The threat echoed the \uc2 PBOC\uc2 's comments in October 2018 when vice governor Pan Gongsheng warned bearish yuan punters not to test the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's mettle. Brazen USD/CNY bulls managed to notch a new 10-year high of 6.9780 a few days later, but the pair then plunged, in part due to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by authorities, but also as U.S. President Trump ordered negotiators to draft a trade deal with China. During the 2018 tussle with punters, China's notable anti-speculative measures included the re-introduction of the counter-cyclical adjustment factor, which has been in full effect recently, and also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the offshore yuan forwards, hiking the cost of short bets against the CNH. This time around, that tactic has not been employed yet.\par \par \uc2 To read our latest \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  news and analysis services, click on\par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-5-30T04:38:19.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190527ef5r00e1l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
