\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -S. Korean won leads gains; stable yuan lends regional support\b0\par\par\uc2 725 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Mai 2019\par 07:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Won touches two-week high\par     * Indian rupee extends gains; close to 3-week peak\par     * Philippine peso bucks trend\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Aby Jose Koilparambil\par     May 27 (Reuters) - Most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose on Monday,\par underpinned by a softer dollar and after a warning from China's\par top banking regulator against betting on the yuan, whose\par stability is vital for its regional peers.\par     Although U.S.-China trade tensions remain the key driving\par theme for markets across assets, emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par started the week on a positive note as the dollar eased.\par     The greenback fell from a two-year high after orders for\par U.S.-made capital goods contracted in further evidence that\par manufacturing and the broader economy are slowing.\par     The weaker-than-expected data, a closely-watched proxy for\par business spending plans, drove the dollar lower and added to a\par fall which began Thursday following a report that showed\par manufacturing activity hit its lowest in almost a decade in May.\par     On Monday, the dollar index was trading slightly\par weaker.\par     Meanwhile, China's banking and insurance regulator said on\par Saturday it did not expect a persistent decline in the yuan\par , while adding that "those who speculate and short the\par yuan will for sure suffer heavy loss".\par     The yuan rose as much as 0.2% to its highest in nearly two\par weeks despite data on Monday showing profits for China's\par industrial firms shrank in April as slowing manufacturing\par activity halted the previous month's surge.\par     Sources had told Reuters \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would use\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and monetary policy tools to stop\par the yuan weakening past the key 7-per-dollar level in the near\par term.\par     "The weaker U.S. durable goods orders data was a negative\par for the dollar, which was helping the Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said\par Chang Wei Liang, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mizuho Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par     Chang added that the Chinese authorities did not want the\par weakness in the yuan to continue and if the unit's stability is\par anchored by policymakers, that would see more strength in Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The yuan has lost more than 2.3% against the dollar since\par the festering China-U.S. trade dispute intensified earlier this\par month.\par     The South Korean won was one among the major\par gainers on the day, appreciating as much as 0.5% to touch a\par two-week peak.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 South Korean finance ministry\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officials too\par had issued verbal warnings last week against disorderly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par market movements as the won weakened to a 2-1/2-year low against\par the dollar.\par     The Indian rupee extended gains for a second\par straight session, strengthening as much as 0.2% to its firmest\par in nearly three weeks, after Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Narendra Modi\f28 \uc2 \f2 's\par ruling party retained power with a massive mandate in the\par general elections.\par     The Taiwan dollar and the Thai baht put on\par up to 0.3%, while the Indonesian rupiah and the\par Malaysian ringgit gained slightly.\par     Bucking the trend, the Philippine peso weakened as\par much as 0.3% to 52.220 against the dollar.\par \par     The following table shows rates for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against\par the dollar at 0511 GMT.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     \par  Japan yen              109.460     109.29    -0.16\par  Sing dlr               1.373       1.3749    +0.11\par  Taiwan dlr             31.429      31.520    +0.29\par  Korean won             1184.000    1188.4    +0.37\par  Baht                   31.780      31.83     +0.16\par  Peso                   52.210      52.09     -0.23\par  Rupiah                 14380.000   14385     +0.03\par  Rupee                  69.500      69.53     +0.04\par  Ringgit                4.185       4.187     +0.06\par  Yuan                   6.893       6.9005    +0.11\par                                               \par  Change so far in 2019                        \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest bid  End 2018  Pct Move\par  Japan yen              109.460     109.56    +0.09\par  Sing dlr               1.373       1.3627    -0.78\par  Taiwan dlr             31.429      30.733    -2.21\par  Korean won             1184.000    1115.70   -5.77\par  Baht                   31.780      32.55     +2.42\par  Peso                   52.210      52.47     +0.50\par  Rupiah                 14380.000   14375     -0.03\par  Rupee                  69.500      69.77     +0.39\par  Ringgit                4.185       4.1300    -1.30\par  Yuan                   6.893       6.8730    -0.29\par  \par \par  (Reporting by Aby Jose Koilparambil in Bengaluru\par Editing by Jacqueline Wong)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-5-27T06:46:21.000Z