\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-UPDATE 1-\uc2 China's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  won't let yuan weaken past 7 to the dollar-sources\b0\par\par\uc2 930 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Mai 2019\par 01:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Repeats for Asian morning readership. No change to text.)               \par \par \uc2 * C.bank eyes steps to slow yuan decline to 7/dollar -sources               \par \par \uc2 * Bill issuance in HK seen signaling bid to curb offshore selling               \par \par \uc2 * Weaker yuan helps China exports, but sharp falls not welcome               \par \par \uc2 * Sharp yuan falls may fuel capital flight, hit stability               \par \par \uc2 By Zheng Li and Kevin Yao               \par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI/BEIJING, May 17 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will use \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and monetary policy tools to stop the yuan weakening past the key 7-per-dollar level in the near-term, three people familiar with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's thinking said.               \par \par \uc2 "At present, rest assured they will certainly not let it break 7," a source told Reuters. A defence of the 7 level could help boost confidence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and soothe investor fears about a sharp depreciation in the yuan, or renminbi, even as souring trade relations with Washington make competitive devaluation a compelling option for Beijing.               \par \par \uc2 "Breaking 7 is beneficial to China because it can reduce some of the effects of tariff increases, but the impact on our renminbi confidence is negative and funds will flow out," the source said.               \par \par \uc2 The yuan fell to its weakest level since December on Friday, and to within striking distance of the 7 mark last seen during the 2008 financial crisis.               \par \par \uc2 It has weakened 3 percent in the past month on fading hopes of a deal being struck in the long-running trade war between Beijing and Washington. The latest flare-up in those tensions saw U.S. President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  increase tariffs on Chinese imports, provoking a similar tariff rise from China.               \par \par \uc2 Although a weaker yuan would support Chinese exporters, the decline would need to be significant to offset the impact of higher U.S. tariffs. Such a fall could in turn fuel capital flight and undermine China's economic stability, policy insiders said. The source told Reuters that China's issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bills in Hong Kong this week was a clear indication the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2 's wanted to soak up offshore yuan to discourage investors from short-selling it.               \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 PBOC\uc2  did not immediately respond to Reuters' request for comment on Friday.               \par \par \uc2 A second source familiar with the \uc2 PBOC\uc2 's thinking said the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  might tolerate the yuan weakening to 7 on fundamental factors but would act to prevent speculative short-selling of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .                              \par \par \uc2 STABILITY VS COMPETITIVENESS               \par \par \uc2 A stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is imperative for China as it seeks to balance its investment-driven economy, attract more portfolio inflows and push for global equity and bond index inclusions.               \par \par \uc2 The tightly managed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell heavily in 2018 and, before that, in 2015 when the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  devalued the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .               \par \par \uc2 The stakes are much higher now, said Bryan Carter, head of emerging market fixed income at \uc2 BNP Paribas Asset Management\uc2  in London.               \par \par \uc2 "A rapid devaluation would shake confidence in the local market and among domestic investors, proving counterproductive," Carter said before Reuters reported source comments on \uc2 PBOC\uc2 . China's balancing act goes beyond maintaining domestic confidence. As the country's current account is seen swinging from a decades-long surplus toward a deficit, the yuan's exchange rate is expected to become more volatile.               \par \par \uc2 A majority of more than 12 money managers, traders and economists Reuters spoke over the past week expected \uc2 PBOC\uc2  to defend the renminbi.               \par \par \uc2 While \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  primarily used direct dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2015, it switched to more unconventional methods such as tightening yuan funding costs and using swaps as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell in 2018.               \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 PBOC\uc2  re-introduced a counter-cyclical factor, a secret component it uses in adjusting the daily reference point for the yuan's trading band, in August last year. Market participants say it has been using that factor to temper depreciation expectations in the past week, by setting a firmer benchmark for yuan than implied by the moves of global \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .               \par \par \uc2 "I don\u8217\'20\'19t believe we will rely on yuan depreciation to boost exports. The yuan is not only for facilitating foreign trade, but it could also affect capital flows," one of the sources said.               \par \par \uc2 "Barring any sharp rise in the dollar, the possibility for a near-term dip in the yuan below 7 is relatively small."               \par \par \uc2 Going against this thinking is market positioning, which points to further weakness.               \par \par \uc2 In the offshore markets, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value one-year out had weakened to 6.9770 per dollar on Friday, slipping from 6.8482 a week ago just before Trump raised tariffs.               \par \par \uc2 A sharp change in the risk-reversal measures in the yuan options market, which indicates the bias towards the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , also showed investors were betting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will weaken.               \par \par \uc2 However, even with these dynamics, there are firmer expectations the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  won't tolerate a sharp selloff.               \par \par \uc2 Liam Spillane, who manages $11.5 billion in emerging market debt for \uc2 Aviva Investors\uc2 , told Reuters he was positioning his portfolio "a little bit more" defensively following renewed escalation in the trade war.               \par \par \uc2 As a result, Spillane has cut exposure in Indonesian government bonds and South African debt while adding small long dollar positions against the Turkish Lira and Taiwanese dollar. At the same time, he is "overweight" the renminbi.               \par \par \uc2 "We've had a long-held belief that Chinese authorities will not allow the renminbi to materially depreciate. We firmly believe they won't use the renminbi as a bargaining tool in the ongoing trade talks with the United States," he said.               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-5-20T00:00:00.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190519ef5j011yp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
