\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Trade tensions boost yen, yuan weakest since Nov\b0\par\par\uc2 728 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2019\par 15:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (New throughout, updates trading and comments to U.S. market\par open, new byline, changes dateline, previous LONDON)\par     By Karen Brettell\par     NEW YORK, May 17 (Reuters) - The safe-haven Japanese yen\par gained on Friday and the offshore Chinese yuan weakened as\par escalating trade tensions between the United States and China\par raised concerns about global growth.\par     The United States must show sincerity if it is to hold\par meaningful trade talks, China said on Friday, after U.S.\par President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  dramatically raised the stakes with a\par potentially devastating blow to Chinese tech giant \f28 \uc2 \f2 Huawei\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par \par     \u8220\'20\'1CRhetoric from both sides is getting more heated, making a\par US-China deal seem a long way off,\u8221\'20\'1D Win Thin, global head of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brown Brothers Harriman\f28 \uc2 \f2  in New York, said\par in a report.\par     \u8220\'20\'1CAt this point, this means there will be no high-level\par negotiations between the two until a potential Trump-Xi\par (Jinping) meeting at the G20 meeting in late June. This means\par the next round of tariffs will likely come into play, signaling\par further escalation and making a deal that much harder,\u8221\'20\'1D Thin\par said.\par     The world's two largest economies are locked in an\par increasingly acrimonious trade dispute that has seen them level\par escalating tariffs on each other's imports in the midst of\par negotiations.\par     The Chinese yuan fell as far as 6.949 against the dollar on\par Friday, its weakest level since Nov. 30.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will use \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par and monetary policy tools to ensure the yuan does not weaken\par past the 7-per-dollar key level in the immediate term, three\par people familiar with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's thinking said.\par \par     The Australian dollar dropped to its lowest level\par since Jan. 3 on the escalating trade tensions.\par     The euro gave back earlier losses against the dollar after\par the White House said that President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  is delaying a\par decision by up to six months on whether to impose tariffs on\par imported cars and parts to allow for more time for trade talks\par with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Japan.\par     The single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been hurt this week by Italian\par Deputy Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Matteo Salvini\f28 \uc2 \f2 's comments that \f28 \uc2 \f2 European\par Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  rules harm the country.\par     Salvini said on Thursday that he would "tear apart" rules\par that are "strangling" Italy if his party scores well in the\par European parliamentary elections next week.\par     Sterling hit a four-month low on Friday after cross-party\par Brexit talks collapsed and concern grew about the impact Prime\par Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Theresa May\f28 \uc2 \f2 's likely resignation would have on\par Britain's exit from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     \par     ========================================================\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 9:04AM (1304 GMT)\par  Description      RIC         Last           U.S. Close  Pct Change     YTD Pct     High Bid    