\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen gains as euro and yuan troubled by European vote and trade\b0\par\par\uc2 552 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2019\par 13:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Dollar dips vs yen on U.S.-China trade woes\par \par \uc2 * Euro weighed down by European election concerns\par \par \uc2 * Offshore yuan at its weakest since November\par \par \uc2 * Graphic: World \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates in 2019 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://tmsnrt.rs/2egbfVh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://tmsnrt.rs/2egbfVh}}}\uc2  (Adds quotes, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Tom Finn\par \par \uc2 LONDON, May 17 (Reuters) - The Japanese yen strengthened on Friday, attracting safe-haven buying amid concerns over trade tensions and impending \uc2 European Parliament\uc2  elections.\par \par \uc2 U.S.-Chinese trade hostilities have had little effect on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but traders have bought the yen, a refuge in times of stress because of Japan's status as the world's largest creditor.\par \par \uc2 "Despite yesterday's rebound, we are still reluctant to trust a long-lasting reversal in risk appetite. With the U.S. (verbally) attacking China, and China willing to respond, we cannot assume that the worst is behind us," said Charalambos Pissouros, a senior market analyst at JFD Brokers.\par \par \uc2 The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was up 0.3% on Friday against the dollar at 109.58 and is up around 1.3% this week.\par \par \uc2 The yen has also benefited from falling government bond yields, which in some cases are now even below the historically low Japanese government borrowing costs.\par \par \uc2 German 10-year bond yields, for example, are now five basis points below the Japanese equivalent for the first time since October 2016.\par \par \uc2 "The yen is the pick of the bunch this week and this month as bond yields have fallen everywhere," Societe Generale \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst Kit Juckes said earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 The euro, meanwhile, is under pressure from worries about next week's European parliamentary elections and comments from Italian Deputy Prime Minister \uc2 Matteo Salvini\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Salvini said on Thursday that he would "tear apart" \uc2 EU\uc2  budget rules that were "strangling" Italy if his party did well in the elections.\par \par \uc2 The euro dropped to its lowest since May 6 and was a touch lower at $1.1158, down 0.6% this week.\par \par \uc2 The dollar has also benefited as a safe-haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  even with the United States and China locked in a trade dispute. It was bolstered on Thursday by data that showed U.S. homebuilding increased more than expected in April.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the dollar held near a two-week high against its peers, supported by the strong data and a bounce in Treasury yields.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index against a basket of six major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  reached 97.921, its highest since May 3.\par \par \uc2 The offshore Chinese yuan weakened to as low as 6.9497 against the dollar, its weakest level since Nov. 30.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will use \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and monetary policy tools to ensure the yuan does not weaken past the 7-per-dollar key level in the immediate term, three people familiar with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's thinking said.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar extended overnight losses and fell to a 4 1/2-month trough of $0.6883. The Aussie fell the previous day after soft domestic employment data raised expectations the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  would cut interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Australia holds a parliamentary election on Saturday, but analysts said U.S.-China tensions were likely to remain the biggest influence on its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Abhinav Ramnarayan, editing by \uc2 Larry King\uc2 ) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-5-17T12:51:39.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190517ef5h01ylp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
