\par\par \b \uc2 China's cbank will not let yuan decline past 7 to the dollar - sources\b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2019\par 09:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI/BEIJING, May 17 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will use \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and monetary policy tools to ensure the yuan does not weaken past the 7-per-dollar key level in the immediate term, three people familiar with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's thinking said.\par \par \uc2 "At present, rest assured they will certainly not let it break 7," a source told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 "Breaking 7 is beneficial to China because it can reduce some of the effects of tariff increases, but the impact on our renminbi confidence is negative and funds will flow out," the source said.\par \par \uc2 The yuan, or renminbi, fell to its weakest level since December on Friday, and to within striking distance of the 7 mark last seen during the 2008 financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 It has weakened 3 percent in the past month on fading hopes of a deal being struck in the long-running trade war between Beijing and Washington. The latest flare-up in those tensions saw U.S. President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  increase tariffs on Chinese imports, provoking a similar tariff rise from China.\par \par \uc2 Although a weaker yuan would support Chinese exporters, the decline would need to be significant to offset the impact of higher U.S. tariffs. Such a fall could in turn fuel capital flight and undermine China's economic stability, policy insiders said. The source told Reuters that China's issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bills in Hong Kong this week was a clear indication of the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2 's intent to soak up offshore yuan and discourage investors from short-selling it.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 PBOC\uc2  did not immediately respond to Reuters' request for comment.\par \par \uc2 A second source familiar with the \uc2 PBOC\uc2 's thinking said the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be fine with the yuan weakening to 7 on fundamental factors but would act to prevent speculative short-selling of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (Additional reporting by Swati Pandey in SYDNEY; Writing by Vidya Ranganathan in SINGAPORE; Editing by Sam Holmes) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-5-17T08:12:40.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190517ef5h00v0r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
