ajor products under each re-structured business lines are as follows: \par  \par  \par Clinical nursing care business includes vascular and non-vascular access infusion devices \par include infusion sets, syringes, puncture needles, specialized single-use clinical collection \par kits; \par  \par  \par  \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 27 Mar 2019 04:51 ET \par HK Bourse: Results Announcement From \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shandong Weigao Group Medical Polymer Co. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  . -10-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par Wound management includes wound healing dressings, wound suture, wound cleaning and \par nonvascular catheter supporting extracorporeal devices; \par  \par  \par Blood management business includes blood collection, storage, separation and sterilization. \par  \par  \par Pharma packaging business includes prefilled syringes and pre-filled flush syringes. \par  \par  \par Medical testing business includes blood collection devices and blood glucose testing. \par  \par  \par Anesthesia and surgery business includes general anesthesia consumables, local anesthesia \par consumables, anesthesia auxiliary consumables, ICU equipment, open and minimally invasive \par surgical equipment. \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                               29 \par Orthopedics business includes trauma, spinal implant, artificial joints, sports injury, soft tissue \par repair, reconstruction implant, orthopedic filling, and orthopedic related surgical tools. \par  \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  products business includes tumor \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , vascular \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  imaging. \par  \par  \par 1.   During the Year, the clinical nursing care business recorded a turnover of approximately \par      RMB3,891,672,000, an overall increase of 8.7% in revenue over last year, the growth \par      is principally due to rich product mix. The Group continued to maintain a dominant \par      position in the market segment. \par  \par  \par 2.   During the Year, the pharma packaging business recorded a turnover of approximately \par      RMB955,609,000, representing an increase of 32.9% over last year and the Company \par      continues to maintain a strong growth momentum. Prefilled syringes have further \par      expanded its market influence in the segment of pre-pack bio-pharmaceuticals and built \par      a broad customer base. Pre-filled flush syringes maintained rapid growth. \par  \par  \par 3.   During the Year, the orthopedics business recorded a turnover of approximately \par      RMB1,180,563,000, representing an increase of 35.6% over last year. Measures such \par      as further consolidating its market position in the spine segment, increased marketing \par      of joint products, further penetration of distribution channels and establishment of a \par      logistic platform have driven sales growth. \par  \par  \par 4.   During the Year, as a result of consolidating products of Argon from the US, the \par      \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  business recorded a turnover of approximately RMB1,444,238,000, \par      representing an increase of 868.6% over last year. The Group will expand sales of Argon \par      products in the PRC market through leveraging resources. \par  \par  \par During the Year, as a result of product mix adjustment, the percentage of turnover from high \par value-added products (products with gross profit margins over 60%) to total turnover was \par about 59.9% (2017: 59.7%). \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                                 30 \par RESEARCH AND DEVELOPMENT \par  \par For the year ended 31 December 2018, the Group obtained 34 new patents and 136 new \par patents are under application in the PRC. Product registration certificates for 65 new \par products were obtained. The research and development for 23 products were completed for \par which application for product registration certificates are underway. For overseas market, 19 \par new patents are under application and the research and development for 47 products were \par completed for which application for product registration certificates are underway. \par  \par  \par The strategy of placing strong emphasis on research and development has enhanced the \par competitiveness and laid a foundation for the Company to fully leverage on its customer \par resources and provided the Group with new profit growth drivers. \par  \par  \par For the year ended 31 December 2018, the Group had over 434 product registration \par certificates and 471 patents, of which 67 were patents on invention, in the PRC. For overseas \par market, the Group had over 584 product registration certificates and 161 patents. \par  \par  \par In view of the need for the strategic adjustments to product mix, the Group continued to \par increase efforts on improvement and subdivision of product layout in existing products series, \par so as to further improve its product series and expand product range. The Group continued to \par maintain the leading position in research and development capability in China. For the year \par ended 31 December 2018, total research and development expenses from continuing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par amounted to approximately RMB311,163,000 (2017: approximately RMB273,825,000), \par representing 3.5% (2017: 4.4%) of the revenue of the Group. \par  \par PRODUCTION \par  \par During the Year, in order to constantly expand production capacity, the Group continued \par to expand its production facilities including workshops of pre-filled flush syringe and pre- \par filled syringe to satisfy the sales demand for future market growth. Meanwhile, the Group \par proactively promoted improvement of production processes and enhanced intellectualization \par  \par and automation of production equipment. The production costs were reduced through \par efficiency enhancement and scientific management, maintaining the Company's overall \par profitability. \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                              31 \par SALES AND MARKETING \par  \par During the Year, the Group consolidated the marketing management system and further \par adhered to the strategy of sales channel integration and product mix adjustment and to focus \par on marketing resources on customer development and maintenance in the core healthcare \par market. The Group achieved substantial results in key client accounts management. As at the \par date of this announcement, the Group newly added 136 hospitals, 57 other medical institutions \par and 68 distributors to its PRC customer base, and the Group has a PRC customer base of \par 5,378 in aggregate (including 2,566 hospitals, 414 blood stations, 644 other medical units \par and 1,754 distributors) and an overseas customer base of 4,418 in aggregate (including 2,873 \par hospitals, 1,377 other medical units and 168 distributors). \par  \par Sales comparison by geographical regions when compared with the last year is set out as \par follows: \par  \par Turnover By Geographical information \par  \par                                                                                     Over \par                                                                            corresponding \par                                                      2018            2017       period % \par                                                   RMB '000        RMB '000 \par Regions \par  \par The PRC \par                                                   3,428,935 \par   -Eastern and Central                                            2,698,118           27.1% \par                                                   