loyees of the Group are resided in Mainland China. During the Year, the \par total cost of salaries, welfare and social benefits of the Group amounted to approximately \par RMB1,456,905,000 (in 2017: approximately RMB1,231,337,000). \par  \par  \par REMUNERATION SYSTEM \par  \par The Group's remuneration policy has been determined based on its performance, changes in \par the local consumption power and competition in human resources market. The remuneration \par policy so determined has become the basis of determining the salary level of employees \par recruited for different positions. The salary of each employee is determined according to \par the employee's performance, ability, employment conditions and the salary standards set by \par  \par the Company. Remuneration of directors is proposed by the Remuneration Committee with \par reference to the operating results of the Company, personal performance of the directors and \par market competition. The proposed remuneration of directors is proposed by the Board subject \par to approval by shareholders at forthcoming annual general meeting. \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                              34 \par FINANCIAL REVIEW \par  \par For the year ended 31 December 2018, the Group recorded a turnover from continuing \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of RMB8,808,861,000, representing an increase of 40.0% over the previous \par financial year. Net profit attributable to the owners of the Company was approximately \par RMB1,472,935,000 (2017: approximately RMB1,728,660,000), representing a decrease of \par approximately 14.8% as compared with the previous year. Net profit attributable to the owners \par of the Company (excluding extraordinary items) was approximately RMB1,586,834,000 \par (2017: approximately RMB1,337,592,000), representing an increase of approximately 18.6% \par over the previous year. \par  \par  \par FINANCIAL SUMMARY \par  \par                 