r ended 31 December 2018, net cash flow from operating activities of the Group \par amounted to approximately RMB2,219,196,000. The Group has maintained a sound cash flow \par position. \par  \par  \par Total interest expenses from continuing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the Group for the year ended \par 31 December 2018 were approximately RMB284,408,000 (2017: approximately \par RMB23,889,000). \par  \par  \par GEARING RATIO \par  \par Due to the acquisition of Argon in January 2018, our gearing ratio as at the end of 2018 \par increased to 36.8% (2017: 7.5%), higher than that for the previous year. \par  \par  \par As at 31 December 2018, total net liabilities of the Group amounted to approximately \par RMB1,525,602,000 (2017: total net cash of RMB2,779,065,000). The gearing ratio which \par represents total debt as a percentage of total capital. Total debt is calculated as total \par borrowings. Total capital is calculated as the Group's shareholders' fund. \par  \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREIGN EXCHANGE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RISKS \par  \par The Group's purchases and sales are mainly conducted in the PRC and the United States. \par Assets, liabilities and transactions in the PRC are denominated in RMB, while overseas assets \par and transactions are mainly denominated in US dollars. For the year ended 31 December \par 2018, the Group had not encountered any material difficulty due to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fluctuation \par nor had it affected its funds for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  purpose. However, due to the relatively long \par repayment cycle with steady revenue in US dollars from overseas subsidiaries, the outstanding \par borrowings in US dollars will not cause significant foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  risk to the Group. \par Notwithstanding, the management will closely monitor risks of exchange rate and consider \par hedging significant \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  risks when necessary. \par  \par  \par Due to the change in exchange rates, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gain from continuing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par equivalent to RMB1,769,000 for the year ended 31 December 2018 was recognised (2017: \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gain equivalent to RMB1,883,000) by the Company. \par  \par  \par  \par                                              36 \par CONTINGENT LIABILITIES \par  \par  \par  \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 27 Mar 2019 04:52 ET \par HK Bourse: Results Announcement From Shandong Weigao Group Medical Polymer Co. Ltd. -12-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par The Group had no material contingent liabilities as at 31 December 2018. \par  \par  \par MATERIAL INVESTMENTS/FUTURE MATERIAL INVESTMENT \par PLANS \par  \par 1.   During the Year, the Group continued to invest approximately RMB651,495,000 for \par      building of properties and production facilities and for the construction of the Group's \par      medical consumables industrial zone. \par  \par  \par 2.   On 23 January 2018, the Group completed the acquisition of Argon through a \par      joint venture formed by Weigao International Medical Company Limited ("Weigao \par      International " ), a subsidiary of the Group, and an independent third party for a \par      consideration of US$850,888,000, of which US$405,443,000 was debt financing raised \par      by Argon. The remaining of US$445,445,000 was funded by Weigao International from \par      its internal resources. \par  \par  \par 3.   In 2019, the Group plans to invest approximately RMB280,000,000 for purchase of \par      new production lines, which are expected to be in production successively by the end of \par      2021. \par  \par 4.   In 2019, the Group plans to further invest approximately RMB150,000,000 for \par      upgrading and reconfiguration of the single-use consumables production equipment to \par      further enhance the level of production automation. \par  \par  \par 5.   It is planned to invest US$40 million in outsourced research and development projects of \par      \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  products to enrich the Company's high-end product line. \par  \par  \par Save for the above material investments and investment plans, the Group had no material \par capital plans or any future plans involving significant investments or capital assets acquisition \par as at 31 December 2018. \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                                37 \par CAPITAL COMMITMENTS \par  \par As at 31 December 2018, the capital commitments of the Group and the Company contracted \par but not provided for in respect of the acquisition of property, plant and equipment and other \par commitments amounted to approximately RMB726,184,000 (2017: RMB2,948,758,000). The \par above amounts will be financed by the internal resources of the Group. \par  \par  \par PLEDGE OF THE GROUP'S ASSETS \par  \par As at 31 December 2018, the Group had pledged the equity interest in Weigao Jierui, a \par wholly-owned subsidiary of the Group, to secure the long-term borrowings from International \par Finance Corporation, and pledged bank deposits of RMB222,270,000 (2017: RMB96,178,000) \par to secure the bills and letters of credit granted to the Group. \par  \par  \par The Financial Leasing Company had pledged accounts receivable of RMB202,983,000 (2017: \par RMB239,589,000) to secure financing. \par  \par  \par The Group had pledged bills receivable of RMB58,029,000 (2017: nil) to secure bank \par facilities. The Group had a security package of 100% equity interests in Argon and its \par subsidiaries as well as the property, plant and equipment, intangible assets, inventories, trade \par and other receivables, bank deposits and cash of Argon to secure the loan with a principal of \par US$420,000,000. \par  \par RESERVES AND DISTRIBUTABLE RESERVES \par  \par As at 31 December 2018, total reserves of the Group amounted to RMB14,062,340,000 (2017: \par RMB12,882,272,000). \par  \par  \par Under the PRC laws and regulations, the Company's distributable reserves will be based on \par the lower of the amount calculated according to the PRC accounting principles and rules and \par the amount calculated according to the Hong Kong generally accepted accounting principles. \par As at 31 December 2018, the distributable reserves of the Company were approximately \par RMB3,824,559,000 (2017: RMB3,391,686,000). \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                               38 \par REVIEW AND OUTLOOK \par  \par During the Year, the Company continued to adhere to product mix optimisation and \par adjustment strategy, accelerated products iteration, and increased investment in engineering \par technologies, with a focus to enhance production efficiency and improve product quality; in \par addition to enhancing the sales management strategy and integrating marketing resources, \par sharing of key accounts as well as implementing staff incentive arrangement, the Company \par continued to maintain growth in revenue and profit despite intensified competition. \par  \par  \par During the Year, the management re-structured and streamlined the product strategy and \par determined on eight major business lines for future development, which extensively covered \par various subdivided markets and explore products with rapid growth, large market and high \par gross profit as main area of focus. Leveraging various resources accumulated over the \par years and efficient management of the Company, the Group continued to consolidate its \par advantageous position in medical device sector in the PRC. \par  \par  \par During the Year, the domestic healthcare industry faced different complicated circumstances \par brought by the continuous deepening medical reform in the PRC. Government policy \par  \par adjustment will be implemented further in various aspects. With profound experience in the \par industry, multi-segments, continual launch of serialized and competitive products as well as \par overseas resources integration, the Group is capable to cope with all risks and challenges. \par  \par LOOKING FORWARD TO 2019 \par  \par Through resources integration, the Company will strengthen product upgrading and research \par and development capabilities. The Company will continue to increase investment in research \par and development, further strengthen existing product lines and intensify the marketing of \par new products. The Company will place more effort to promote product safety and patient \par application safety, improve patient treatment experience and quicken the pace in launching \par pipeline products, which could help to offset numerous adverse impacts and to maintain its \par competitive edge. \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                              39 \par In view of the effectiveness achieved by key client accounts management, the Company will \par continue to focus on such strategy and increase single customer contribution by promoting \par various products via the key accounts management \par  \par  \par The in-depth implementation of national medical reform policies may cause fluctuations \par in the financial performance to a certain extent in the short term but will facilitate industry \par concentration and increase the market share of excellent brands in the long-term and benefit \par the rapid growth of leading enterprises in the industry. \par  \par  \par As overseas market is the focus of our medium and long-term strategic plan, the Company \par will proactively develop its overseas business layout and proceed with sales of marketable \par product in target market, and it will gradually establish long-term stable sales channel and \par network. The proportion of sales in overseas markets to the total revenue of the Group is \par expected to increase gradually. \par  \par  \par On 23 January 2018, WW Medical and Healthcare Holdings Corporation("WW Holding"), \par the Group's 89.8% owned subsidiary, acquired 100% of the shares of Argon for consideration \par of USD850,888,001(equivalent to RMB5,446,449,000). Argon is principally engaged in \par the production and sale of medical devices for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  radiology, vascular surgery, \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cardiology and oncology. At the strategic level, Argon will become the Group's \par platform for overseas expansion and play an active role in technological upgrade, product \par innovation and mergers and acquisitions. At the business \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  level, the Group will \par work with the management team of Argon to implement the sale of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  products in \par the market in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The management considers that Argon as an important business unit of \par Weigao will make contributions to the long-term stable development of the Group. \par  \par  \par While continuously carrying out engineering technologies, automation and supply chain \par management improvement in production, the Company will continue to improve its product \par quality and to, increase production efficiency to maintain cost advantages. \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                               40 \par By relying on its extensive strategic layout in the business fields and high quality products \par and insistence on adapting to market and future-oriented operating strategy and motivation \par of employee creativity, the management believes that the Company will continue to maintain \par its leading position in the PRC market. Meanwhile, the Company will proactively develop \par overseas business to achieve the coordinated development of domestic and foreign markets, \par supporting the stable growth in the operating results of the Group. \par  \par  \par Argon will become the Group's platform for overseas expansion and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  product \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  expansion. \par  \par PURCHASE, SALE OR REDEMPTION OF THE COMPANY'S LISTED \par SECURITIES \par  \par During the Year, there was no purchase, sale or redemption of its securities by the Company or \par any of its subsidiaries. \par  \par  \par BOARD PRACTICES AND PROCEDURES \par  \par The Code on Corporate Governance Practices (the "CCGP") contained in the Listing Rules \par which set out the principles of good corporate governance and the Company is required \par to comply with the code provisions of the CCGP. The Company fully admitted that good \par corporate governance, as part of the Company's culture, can create values to the Group and \par the Shareholders efficiently. The Board is committed to continuing to enhance the standards of \par corporate governance within the Group and to ensure that the Group conducts its businesses \par in an honest and responsible manner. The Group has adopted practices which meets the code \par provisions of the CCGP. \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                               41 \par CHANGE OF BOARD COMPOSITION AND SENIOR MANAGEMENT \par  \par       Mr. Wang Yi ("Mr. Wang"), an executive director, has been re-designated as a non- \par (1) \par  \par  \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 27 Mar 2019 04:52 ET \par HK Bourse: Results Announcement From Shandong Weigao Group Medical Polymer Co. Ltd. -13-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \