ngs of such review to the Board and the audit committee. The Board has conducted a \par review of the effectiveness of the system of internal control of the Group. \par  \par  \par SCOPE OF WORK OF MESSRS. DELOITTE TOUCHE TOHMATSU \par  \par The figures in respect of the Group ' s consolidated statement of financial position, \par consolidated statement of profit or loss and other comprehensive income and the related notes \par thereto for the year ended 31 December 2018 as set out in the preliminary announcement have \par been agreed by the Group's auditor, Messrs. Deloitte Touche Tohmatsu, to the amounts set out \par in the Group's audited consolidated financial statements for the year. The work performed by \par Messrs. Deloitte Touche Tohmatsu in this respect did not constitute an assurance engagement \par in accordance with Hong Kong Standards on Auditing, Hong Kong Standards on Review \par Engagements or Hong Kong Standards on Assurance Engagements issued by the Hong Kong \par Institute of Certified Public Accountants and consequently no assurance has been expressed \par by Messrs. Deloitte Touche Tohmatsu on the preliminary announcement. \par  \par AUDIT COMMITTEE \par  \par The Audit Committee of the Company comprises three independent non-executive directors, \par namely Mr. Lo Wai Hung, Mrs. Fu Ming Zhong and Mrs. Wang Jin Xia and one non-executive \par Director, namely Mrs. Zhou Shu Hua. The Chairman of the Audit Committee is Mr. Lo \par Wai Hung. The Audit Committee has reviewed the Group's audited consolidated financial \par statements for the Year which have been agreed by the Company's auditor, and is of the \par view that the Group's audited consolidated financial statements for the Year are prepared in \par accordance with the applicable accounting standards, laws and regulations, and appropriate \par disclosures have already been made. The Audit Committee has also reviewed the annual \par results for the Year. \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                               43 \par CONFIRMATION OF INDEPENDENCE OF THE INDEPENDENT NON \par EXECUTIVE DIRECTORS \par  \par The Company confirmed that it had received the annual confirmation of independence from \par each of the Independent Non-executive Directors in compliance with Rule 3.13 of the Listing \par Rules for the year ended 31 December 2018. The Company is of the view that the Independent \par Non-executive Directors remain independent during the Year in accordance with the relevant \par requirements of Rule 3.13 of the Listing Rules. \par  \par  \par PRE-EMPTIVE RIGHTS \par  \par There are no provisions for pre-emptive right under the Company's articles of association and \par the laws of the PRC, which would oblige the Company to offer new shares on a pro-rata basis \par to existing shareholders. \par  \par CORPORATE GOVERNANCE \par  \par The Company is committed to maintain high standards of corporate governance so as to \par ensure better transparency and protection of shareholders ' interest. The Company has \par complied with the code provision of the Code on Corporate Governance Practices (the \par "Code") in Appendix 14 of the Listing Rules throughout the year ended 31 December 2018. \par  \par  \par ANNUAL GENERAL MEETING AND CLOSURE OF REGISTER OF \par MEMBERS \par  \par  \par Attending and Voting in the Annual General Meeting \par  \par  \par In order to determine the shareholders who are entitled to attend and vote at the Annual \par General Meeting, the register of members of the Company will be closed from Saturday, \par 1 June 2019 to Tuesday, 2 July 2019 (both days inclusive), during which period no transfer of \par H Shares will be effected. In order to qualify for attending and voting in the Annual General \par Meeting, Shareholders should ensure that all transfer documents, accompanied by the relevant \par share certificates, are lodged with the Company's H Share registrar, Tricor Standard Limited, \par at Level 22, Hopewell 