on no later than 4:30 p.m. \par on Monday, 8 July 2019. \par  \par  \par In order to qualify to entitle the final dividend for the year ended 31 December 2018:- \par  \par Latest time to lodge in transfer instrument accompanied \par   by the share certificates for H Shares . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 4:30 p.m., Monday, \par                                                                                                     8 July 2019 \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                                         45 \par Closure of register of members of \par   the Company for entitlement of \par   the final dividend for the \par   year ended 31 December 2018. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . Tuesday, 9 July 2019 to \par                                                                                          Sunday, 14 July 2019 \par                                                                                           (both day inclusive) \par  \par Record date for the entitlement of \par   the final dividend . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . Sunday, 14 July 2019 \par  \par Expected despatch date of the final dividend. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . Thursday, 15 August 2019 \par  \par The final dividend will be despatched at the risk of those entitled thereto to their respective \par registered addresses on or before Thursday, 15 August 2019. \par  \par PROPOSED FINAL DIVIDEND \par  \par The Board proposed the distribution of a final dividend for the year ended 31 December \par 2018 of RMB0.052 (2017: RMB0.046) (before considering any tax effect) per share totaling \par RMB235,161,000 (2017: RMB208,027,000), which will be subject to the approval of \par shareholders of the Company at the forthcoming 2018 annual general meeting. Dividend \par payable to Shareholders will be declared in Renminbi and paid in Hong Kong dollars, the \par exchange rate of which will be calculated based on the average exchange rate published by \par The People's Bank of China during the week prior to the Annual General Meeting. Subject \par to the approval of the Annual General Meeting, the 2018 final dividend will be paid on \par 15 August 2019. \par  \par In accordance with the Enterprise Income Tax Law of the People's Republic of China ( \par ) and its implementation rules effective on 1 January 2008, \par where a PRC domestic enterprise distributes dividends for financial periods beginning \par  \par  \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 27 Mar 2019 04:52 ET \par HK Bourse: Results Announcement From Shandong Weigao Group Medical Polymer Co. Ltd. -14-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par from 1 January 2008 to non-resident enterprise shareholders, it is required to withhold \par 10% enterprise income tax for such non-resident enterprise shareholders. Therefore, as a \par PRC domestic enterprise, the Company will, after withholding 10% of the final dividend as \par enterprise income tax, distribute the final dividend to non-resident enterprise shareholders, i.e. \par any shareholders who hold the Company's shares in the name of non-individual shareholders, \par including but not limited to HKSCC Nominees Limited, other nominees, trustees, or holders \par of H Shares registered in the name of other organizations and groups. \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                                            46 \par                                                  the \par Pursuant to the PRC Individual Income Tax Law                                              , \par  \par Implementation Regulations of the PRC Individual Income Tax Law \par  the Notice of the State Administration of Taxation in relation to \par                            , \par the Administrative Measures on Preferential Treatment Entitled by Non-residents under Tax \par  \par Treaties (Tentative) (Guo Shui Fa [2009] No. 124) \par                        [2009]124 (the "Tax Treaties \par                                                                         ) \par Notice"), the Notice of the State Administration of Taxation on the Questions Concerning the \par Levy and Administration of Individual Income Tax After the Repeal of Guo Shui Fa [1993] \par                                                      [1993]045 \par No. 45 (Guo Shui Han [2011] No. 348) \par                    [2011]348 , other relevant laws \par  \par and regulations and other regulatory documents, the Company shall, as a withholding agent, \par withhold and pay individual income tax for the individual holders of H shares in respect \par of the dividend to be distributed to them. However, the individual holders of H shares may \par be entitled to certain tax preferential treatments pursuant to the tax treaties between the \par PRC and the countries (regions) in which the individual holders of H shares are domiciled \par and the tax arrangements between Mainland China, Hong Kong or Macau. For individual \par holders of H shares in general, the Company will withhold and pay individual income tax \par at the rate of 10% on behalf of the individual holders of H shares in the distribution of the \par dividend. However, the tax rates applicable to individual holders of H Shares overseas may \par vary depending on the tax treaties between the PRC and the countries (regions) in which \par the individual holders of H shares are domiciled, and the Company will withhold and pay \par individual income tax on behalf of the individual holders of H shares in the distribution of the \par dividend accordingly. \par  \par The Company will identify the country of domicile of the individual holders of H shares \par according to their registered address on the H share register of members of the Company \par (the "Registered Address"). If the domicile of an individual holders of H shares is not the \par same as the Registered Address or if the individual holders of H shares would like to apply \par for a refund of the additional amount of tax finally withheld and paid, the individual holders \par of H shares shall notify and provide relevant supporting documents to the Company. Upon \par examination of the supporting documents by the relevant tax authorities, the Company will \par follow the guidance given by the tax authorities to implement the relevant tax withholding \par provisions and arrangements. Individual holders of H shares may either personally or appoint \par a representative to attend to the procedures in accordance with the requirements under the Tax \par Treaties Notice if they do not provide the relevant supporting documents to the Company. \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                               47 \par The Company assumes no responsibility and disclaims all liabilities whatsoever in relation \par to the tax status or tax treatment of the individual holders of H shares and for any claims \par arising from or in connection with any delay in or inaccurate determination of the tax status \par or tax treatment of the individual holders of H shares or any disputes over the withholding \par mechanism or arrangements. \par  \par Shareholders are recommended to consult their tax advisors regarding the PRC, Hong Kong \par and other tax implications arising from or in connection with their holding and disposal of the \par H shares of the Company. \par  \par PUBLICATION OF FINANCIAL RESULTS ON THE WEBSITE OF THE \par STOCK EXCHANGE \par  \par This announcement is available for viewing on the websites of the Stock Exchange and the \par Company. The annual report of the Company for the year ended 31 December 2018 will be \par  \par dispatched to shareholders of the Company and published on the Stock Exchange and the \par Company's websites respectively in due course. \par  \par  \par  \par Source: Hong Kong Exchanges & Clearing \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 March 27, 