\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  gain on Fed's more cautious stance\b0\par\par\uc2 823 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2019\par 06:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Indonesian rupiah hits 3-wk high\par     * Chinese yuan at more than 8-month high\par     * Thai Feb exports rise 5.9 pct y/y\par     * Indonesia, Philippine, Taiwan rate decisions expected, all\par seen\par on hold \par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Shriya Ramakrishnan\par     March 21 (Reuters) - Emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  firmed on\par Thursday as the dollar weakened after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par surprised markets by bringing its three-year tightening drive to\par an earlier than expected end.  \par     The Fed on Wednesday abandoned plans for any interest rate\par hikes this year amid signs of an economic slowdown, and said it\par would halt the steady decline of its balance sheet in September.\par \par     The Indonesian rupiah strengthened as much as 0.6\par percent against the dollar, touching its highest level since\par Feb. 28. The rupiah has outperformed its peers by a vast margin\par this year after declining nearly 6 percent in 2018. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  is due to release a policy decision later in\par the day, and is widely expected to keep interest rates unchanged\par for a fourth straight month.\par     Indonesia's finance minister said on Thursday that the Fed's\par forecast for no rate hikes in 2019 "will be good for global\par economy" as markets will be calmer than in 2018, when the U.S.\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  raised rates four times.\par     "The dovish Fed surprise may trigger a bullish re-think of\par ranges for emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets. However, a sustained\par bullish break-out may still be contingent on a U.S.-China\par (trade) deal with a potential \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stability clause\par especially for Chinese yuan and allied \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," economists\par at Citi said in a note.\par     "In the meantime, high yielding Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may outperform."\par     The South Korean won strengthened 0.3 percent, in\par tandem with the local equity benchmark index, while the\par Taiwan dollar edged higher.\par     Central banks in Taiwan and the Philippines are also\par expected to leave rates unchanged later in the day, with\par investors looking for any hints of future easing after the Fed\par decision.\par     Meanwhile on the trade front, U.S. President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par warned on Wednesday that the United States may leave tariffs on\par Chinese goods for a "substantial period" to ensure Beijing\par complies with any trade agreement.\par     U.S.-China trade talks are set to resume in Beijing next\par week, the first face-to-face talks since Trump delayed a March 1\par deadline to avert a rise in tariffs on $200 billion worth of\par Chinese imports.\par     The Thai baht appreciated 0.2 percent, after data\par released on Thursday showed that the country's customs-cleared\par exports unexpectedly rose in February, after contracting for\par three consecutive months.\par     Indian financial markets were closed for a public holiday.\par     \par     CHINESE YUAN    \par     The Chinese yuan strengthened as much as 0.4\par percent, rising to an over eight-month high against the dollar.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Thursday lifted it official yuan\par midpoint to the strongest level in eight months at 6.6850 per\par dollar. \par     "While the comments from Trump on the trade front suggest\par that there is still a risk we might not get a deal, for now\par markets have brushed it aside," Khoon Goh, head of Asia research\par at \f28 \uc2 \f2 ANZ Banking Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  (Singapore) said. \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been a point of contention among U.S. and\par Chinese officials during trade talks, with Washington seeking\par assurance China will not depreciate its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to offset the\par impact of any U.S. measures.\par     Earlier this month, People's Bank Of China Governor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Yi Gang\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par said that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has exited from regular\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will absolutely\par not use the exchange root to boost its exports.\par     \par     \par     The following table shows rates for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against\par the dollar at 0457 GMT.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest bid  Previous day  Pct Move\par  Japan yen              110.480     110.68        +0.18\par  Sing dlr               1.347       1.3468        -0.01\par  Taiwan dlr             30.810      30.833        +0.07\par  Korean won             1126.600    1130.4        +0.34\par  Baht                   31.660      31.73         +0.22\par  Peso                   52.840      52.81       