\par\par \b \uc2 Yuan's drop aligns it with China's cooling economy, easier policy\b0\par\par\uc2 890 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 2019\par 04:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI/HONG KONG, Jan 22 (Reuters) - A surprising rally for China's yuan over the turn of the year has been cut short by widespread expectations that Beijing will ramp up policy easing in coming months to avert a sharper economic slowdown.\par \par \uc2 The yuan has retreated to the weaker side of 6.8 per dollar this week, but is still up nearly 3 percent since early December on hopes that Washington and Beijing may be inching toward a trade deal.\par \par \uc2 Gains in a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that was one of Asia's weakest in 2018 were also fueled by expectations that Beijing does not want to see the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  drop too much, in case it becomes a sticking point in negotiations with the Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 But analysts say mere optimism over trade talks cannot take it any higher, unless it's driven by a dramatic decline in the dollar. Caution over trade and the extent of further Chinese easing are likely to cap the yuan's gains.\par \par \uc2 Trade negotiators are facing an early March deadline and Washington has threatened to sharply hike tariffs on Chinese goods if there are no substantial signs of compromise from Beijing. nL1N1ZI1KR]\par \par \uc2 "If we look back, the three factors driving renminbi depreciation, including dollar appreciation, the trade war and interest rate differentials last year, only dollar appreciation has turned," said \uc2 Tommy Xie\uc2 , an economist at OCBC Bank in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 Uncertainties over trade, China's slowdown and policy easing would cause the yuan's yield differences with the dollar to narrow, and place it under pressure, he said.\par \par \uc2 Stefan Hofer, chief investment strategist at the Hong Kong branch of private bank LGT, expects the yuan to weaken to 6.9 in three months and then recover to 6.7 in 12 months.\par \par \uc2 Hofer said \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should prioritise restoring investor confidence in its capital markets, in particular its equity markets which plunged last year. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability is key to that, he says.\par \par \uc2 Analysts at \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  said last week that they had turned bullish on the yuan, both because the \uc2 People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  (PBOC) \uc2 would refrain from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  during trade talks and as companies convert more dollars into yuan ahead of Lunar New Year payments.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell more than 5 percent in 2018, and at one point had looked set break through a decade-low of 7 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Andy Seaman, chief investment officer at Stratton Street in London, is long the yuan, even though his fund mainly buys Chinese dollar bonds rather than the domestic ones.\par \par \uc2 He says the yuan's fundamentals do not justify its weakness and it was weak only because of the dollar's broad strength.\par \par \uc2 Authorities are also likely to want to keep the yuan stable ahead of China's debut in global bond indexes. A phased inclusion of yuan-denominated government debt in the Bloomberg Barclays Global Aggregate Index is scheduled for April.\par \par \uc2 GRAVITY DEFYING\par \par \uc2 Even yuan bulls concede its recent gains have been gravity-defying, with some China watchers saying the economy may be in the midst of a significant slowdown.\par \par \uc2 Data on Monday showed fourth-quarter economic growth cooled to 6.4 percent on-year, the weakest since the global financial crisis. That dragged full-year 2018 growth to 6.6 percent, the weakest in 28 years.\par \par \uc2 Growth is set to cool further this year, with some analysts predicting it could drop below 6 percent this spring, before support measures start to stabilise activity around mid-year.\par \par \uc2 Stuart Ritson, portfolio manager for emerging market debt at \uc2 Aviva Investors\uc2 , noted the yuan had rallied despite obvious risks, including a decline in the current account surplus.\par \par \uc2 "I'm just not too sure as a policy tool, given the sensitivity during the trade talks, that it's possible to really allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken too much."\par \par \uc2 HEADWINDS\par \par \uc2 Most analysts polled by Reuters at the beginning of this year believe the yuan will weaken below 7 within six months.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say the yuan's strength gives the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  room to cut interest rates and pump cash into markets, a change from last year when capital outflow risks were a key concern as yields fell and the yuan was weakening.\par \par \uc2 Despite losing its yield advantage over dollar rates, outflows were moderate in 2018, with only a modest drop in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 But falling local yields could drag on the yuan later this year. While the Fed has now hinted future rate rises may be slower, U.S. yields are still rising. Chinese three-month yields are now 11 basis points below U.S. yields, a sharp turn from being 250 points higher early in 2018.\par \par \uc2 "Even though there is no basis for yuan depreciation, there is no basis for a unilateral appreciation either," said Stephen Chiu, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  and rates strategist at \uc2 China Construction Bank\uc2  (Asia) in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2 China might be willing to let the yuan fall if that depreciation was justified by fundamentals, such as unexpected weakness in the economy, Chiu said.\par \par \uc2 But China's key priority this year was to stabilise market expectations, and encouraging any yuan depreciation would be viewed as comprehensive monetary easing, he said.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 6.7732 Chinese yuan) (Editing by Vidya Ranganathan & Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-1-22T04:55:26.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190122ef1m009st\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
