\par\par \b \uc2 Market Talk Roundup: Latest on Trump, U.S. Politics\b0\par\par\uc2 1,644 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 2018\par 15:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 The latest Market Talks covering President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and U.S. politics. Published exclusively on Dow Jones Newswires throughout the day.\par \par \uc2 0924 ET - Adding to the ferrous pressure on London base metals are remarks from President Trump in an interview with The Wall Street Journal that it was "highly unlikely" that he would accept Beijing's request to hold off on increasing tariff rates on Chinese goods from the beginning of January 2019. Speaking ahead of his scheduled meeting with Chinese counterpart \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2  on the sidelines of this week's \uc2 Group of 20\uc2  nations summit in Buenos Aires, Mr. Trump said that while he would only accept a deal that opened China's markets to competition from U.S. companies, he also expected to "make a great deal with China." The prospective meeting between the U.S. and Chinese leaders will be in investors' sights, as will any communication between Russian and Saudi leaders regarding oil production. ( david.hodari@wsj.com ; @davidhodari)\par \par \uc2 0851 ET - The ruble has clawed back much of the ground it lost after Russia seized three Ukrainian naval ships on Sunday, raising the threat of hostilities between the neighbors and the possibility of another round of Western sanctions on Moscow. But \uc2 Piotr Matys\uc2  , an \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  , says the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains vulnerable despite Tuesday's rally, particularly since Russia's economy faces another headwind in the form of falling oil prices. "This incident raises the chances of sanctions being imposed on Russia at a time when economic growth already seems to be weakening," he said. The ruble slumped in 2014 when Russia was hit with Western sanctions after annexing Crimea. It last trades 0.5% higher against the dollar; the MOEX Russia stock index is up 0.6%.(joe.wallace@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0744 ET - US stock futures weaker after Monday's 354 point Dow rally as investors react to comments from President Trump that the US could put tariffs on \uc2 Apple\uc2  iPhones and laptop computers imported from China. The remarks came in a WSJ interview ahead of Trump's meeting with China's President \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2  later this week at the \uc2 Group of 20\uc2  summit in Buenos Aires. \uc2 Apple\uc2  shares off 2% in premarket trading. In corporate news, \uc2 United Technologies\uc2  will spin off its \uc2 Otis\uc2  division and Carrier building systems businesses, leaving UTC a pure-play aerospace company. \uc2 Salesforce\uc2  is expected to report 3Q results after the bell. Investors will look for signs of whether strong corporate-tech buying has eased amid the US-China trade dispute and slowing global growth. S&P futures are down 8.50 points. (patrick.sheridan@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0740 ET - Russia has unveiled plans to issue euro-denominated government debt, according to media reports citing officials at \uc2 Russia's finance ministry\uc2  . Russia would be issuing a bond with a seven-year maturity and 3% yield in a benchamark-size transaction, the reports say. The move could be an effort to reduce exposure to debt issued in U.S. dollars in light of a possible new wave of U.S. sanctions as tensions between Washington and Moscow escalate. On Monday, U.S. United Nations Ambassador Nikki Haley criticized Russia at an Emergency Security Council and called for the release of Ukrainian ships and crew seized by Russia over the weekend. Mrs Haley didn't elaborate on whether the U.S was considering ramping up sanctions against Moscow.(lorena.ruibal@wsj.com; @lorena_rbal)\par \par \uc2 0728 ET - Sterling at $1.27 is pricing in both "the hope of some workable compromise and the threat of a hard Brexit," says \uc2 Boris Schlossberg\uc2 , managing director of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at BK Asset Management. On Tuesday, the pound is last down by 0.5% at 1.2744, having fallen to a 12-day low of 1.2728. "For now, the market continues to hold above that level [1.27] as the consensus view is that some sort of a soft exit [from the EU ] will be worked out." "But, with U.K. parliament appearing ready to vote down the deal, and with no credible alternatives left, the prospect of a hard Brexit has become uncomfortably real as the deadline looms," Mr. Schlossberg says. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0708 ET - The Turkish lira has recovered nearly all losses it made in August and \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  analyst \uc2 Antje Praefcke\uc2  says this is "somewhat disturbing." USD/TRY is last down by 0.2% at 5.2368 on Tuesday after it fell to a 16-week low of 5.2180 on Monday, according to \uc2 FactSet\uc2 . The rise in the lira comes as U.S.-Turkey tensions and U.S.-Chinese trade tensions ease, while lower oil prices have helped. But real interest rates are negative in Turkey, with inflation above \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates. In October inflation rose to 25.24% and is expected to have risen in November as well, \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  says. "Doubts...remain as to whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  really has reverted back to a pro-active monetary policy," the bank says. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0608 ET - Concerns about the risk of U.S. sanctions due to tensions between Russia and Ukraine mean the ruble is likely to fall further and USD/RUB could rise to 70, says \uc2 MUFG\uc2 . USD/RUB earlier rose to a two-week high of 67.23, before the ruble recovered some of its losses leaving USD/RUB last down 0.8% at 66.6381. The ruble fell on worries that the U.S. may impose new sanctions on Russia after three Ukrainian naval ships and their crews were captured under gunfire by Russia on Monday. "It is reportedly the most serious maritime incident since the 2014 invasion of Crimea," \uc2 MUFG\uc2  says. "It comes at a time when President Trump is currently considering implementing a second phase of penalties in response to the Novichok attack in the U.K." (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0528 ET - The dollar rose this year as investors bought the most liquid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in preparation of trade wars. But its rise also reflected a belief that the U.S. economy would "remain largely unscathed by trade tension," says \uc2 MUFG\uc2 , a view that could be undermined if data turn weaker. "There is scope for that perception to change as U.S. growth is likely to slow next year," \uc2 MUFG\uc2  says. So far the negative impact of trade tensions has been more evident overseas where growth has slowed, whereas fiscal stimulus has helped to lift U.S. growth this year. But, the "recent weakness in the U.S. equity market could be an early warning signal." (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0512 ET - The dollar likely will rise versus the Chinese yuan and the \uc2 People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely "will gear up for more \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect 7 [level in USD/CNY] until 2019," says \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  . U.S. President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is due to meet China President \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2  at the G20 summit, which starts on Friday. The two leaders are expected to discuss trade relations and hopes are fading that Mr. Trump will abandon the aim to raise tariffs to 25% from 10% on Chinese imports from January. "The bar is low for a positive surprise," SocGen says. "The dollar has weakened after the last two G20 summits," and the "stakes this time are considerably higher." USD/CNY is last up 0.1% at 6.9490. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0340 ET - The uncertainty over whether the U.K. parliament will vote down the Brexit withrawal deal continues to weigh on the pound, which falls to a 12-day low of $1.2728. The vote is due for Dec. 12 and analysts have warned that sterling is likely to be volatile in the next couple of weeks. U.S. President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  's comments add to the pressure, with Mr. Trump reportedly suggesting Theresa May 's Brexit agreement could threaten a U.S.-U.K. trade deal. This goes against the insistance of Mrs. May's team that it was "very clear" the U.K. would be able to sign trade deals with countries around the world, the BBC reported. EUR/GBP is up 0.4% at 0.8873. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0313 ET - The dollar is flat on Tuesday, despite U.S. President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  saying in an interview with the WSJ that he expected to go ahead with increasing tariff levels on $200 of Chinese goods to 25% next year, as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains largely unimpeded by trade tensions. Trump also said he would put tariffs on remaining Chinese imports if negotiations weren't favorable for the U.S. RBC says this statement is "seen as part and parcel of Trump's negotiating style, piling on the pressure ahead of a crucial meeting," at the G20 summit, which starts on Friday. The DXY dollar index trades flat at 97.11. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0239 ET - The FTSE 100 index is expected to open 6 points lower at 7030, \uc2 London Capital Group\uc2  says, as hopes of breakthrough in U.S.-China trade talks at the upcoming G20 summit fade, leaving investors risk-averse. U.S. President Trump said he expects to go ahead with increasing tariffs on Chinese imports to 25% in January. "His comments reflect how little progress has been made in trade talks so far and highlights the low probability for any deal to be agreed with China's President Xi," says \uc2 Jasper Lawler\uc2 , analyst at LCG. Weaker oil prices may hurt heavyweight oil stocks while travel-related stocks may suffer after holiday company Thomas Cook gave a profit warning for FY 2018 and suspended its dividend. (jessica.fleetham@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 27, 2018 09:24 ET (14:24 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020181127eebr001jk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
