\par\par \b \uc2 Global  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  and Fixed Income Roundup: Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,609 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 2018\par 11:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 The latest Market Talks covering \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Fixed Income. Published exclusively on Dow Jones Newswires throughout the day.\par \par \uc2 0933 GMT - The fall in the Chinese yuan to a 10-year low against the U.S. dollar overnight "will only exacerbate" the trade spat between the U.S. and China, "as the Trump administration will view the price action as an attempt to offset the costs caused by [U.S.] tariffs," says \uc2 Boris Schlossberg\uc2 , managing director of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at BK Asset Management. USD/CNY rose to a 10-year high of 6.9646 overnight in Asia, shying away from the key 7 level. USD/CNY is last flat at 6.9437. "Given the fact that U..S goods trade deficits widened for the fourth month in a row, the Trump administration's policy on trade is clearly not working and today's action on USD/CNY exchange rates will only make markets more nervous that further retaliation will follow soon," Mr. Schlossberg says. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0854 GMT - The Singapore dollar fell to a 3-week low against the US dollar late in Asia Friday, amid gains by the greenback against most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The USD/SGD was at 1.3825 vs 1.3800 previous close. Intraday, the pair touched a high of 1.3846, the highest since Oct. 8. Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reiterated that the local economy is set to slow a bit, though will stay on an "enduring" growth path in coming quarters. That is likely to cap any gains in the USD, with resistance currently seen near 1.3860. (gaurav.raghuvanshi@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0841 GMT - Yuan rate rebounded against the U.S. dollar in late trading after a \b \highlight22\uc2 China central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy chief signalled there could be more \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Beijing if the yuan weakens further. "As for those forces that have tried short selling the renminbi, we fought against each other years ago...The memory should remain fresh for all of us," says Pan Gongsheng at a briefing. The \uc2 PBoC\uc2  can't afford a free fall in yuan rate due to rising capital outflow concerns, \uc2 Citi\uc2  says. The yuan regained some ground onshore against the U.S. dollar after slipping below 6.95 and is now trading around 6.94.(liyan.qi@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0828 GMT - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Russia\uc2  announces its interest rate decision Friday, and is likely to keep its key rate on hold at the 7.5%, analysts say. This is justified by the fact that "inflation is in line with the year-end target, the economy isn't overheated and markets have calmed down in the last six weeks," says ING. As a result, the Russian ruble is likely to remain around same levels on Friday and into year-end, it says. The ruble is last slightly weaker against the dollar, with USD/RUB up 0.2% at 65.6735. But "the risks are that we see a stronger ruble." The \uc2 CBR\uc2 's decision in December is unclear yet. The announcement is due at 1030 GMT. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0810 GMT - Following data that showed Malaysia's inflation was lower than expected in September, ANZ says it sees underlying inflation remaining low and stable through 1H of next year. Combined with more moderate economic activity and external factors such as trade tensions, ANZ says it expects \uc2 Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the overnight policy rate unchanged at 3.25% for some time. ( yantoultra.ngui@wsj.com ; @yantoultra)\par \par \uc2 0752 GMT - Government bond supply in the eurozone will be very subdued next week, with only Italy lining up for a government bond auction, scheduled Tuesday. "The Italian solo will nonetheless ensure a strong focus on primary as markets look for tangible signals for underlying investor demand for BTPs," say \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  's rates strategists. Italy's treasury will offer EUR1.5 billion to EUR2 billion in the 2.45% October 2023 BTP, EUR2 billion to EUR2.5 billion in the 2.80% December 2028 BTP and EUR500 million to EUR1 billion in the September 2025 CCTeu, a floating rate note. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0751 GMT Currently trading at 151.84, the French December OAT contract is on the upside and remains supported by its rising 50-period moving average at 151.62 on a 30-minute chart. In addition, the 14 period RSI on a 30-minute chart stands within its buying area between 50 and 70 and confirms the bullish bias. As a consequence, above horizontal support at 151.47, further advance is expected with a first target set at strong horizontal resistance at 152.00. The upside breakout of this threshold would open the way toward strong horizontal resistance and overlap at 152.25 and toward Sept. 6 top at 152.50 in extension. Only a break below horizontal support at 151.47 would invalidate this bullish view and would favour a weakness toward previous overlap at 151.34 and toward horizontal support at 151.10 in extension. [This piece contains the opinions of Trading Central and does not constitute personalized investment advice or form part of any invitation or inducement to buy or sell any security. The author has been prohibited by Trading Central from purchasing or otherwise directly or indirectly acquiring any direct or indirect beneficial ownership of any instruments or markets for which Trading Central or its affiliates issues recommendations. To read more, visit bit.ly/1MehCU9.] (analysts-europe@tradingcentral.com)\par \par \uc2 0748 GMT Currently trading at $1.1377, the euro is on the downside, capped by its declining 50-period moving average at $1.1384 on a 30-minute chart. From a technical point of view, the 14-period RSI stands within its buying area between 50 and 70 and confirms the bullish bias. As a consequence, as long as $1.1360 holds as horizontal resistance, further weakness is expected toward horizontal support at $1.1330 at first and toward August bottom at $1.1300 in extension. A third target is set at $1.1280. Only a rebound above horizontal resistance at $1.1395 would invalidate this bearish view and favour a rise toward horizontal resistance and overlap at $1.1430 and even toward horizontal resistance at $1.1450 in extension. [This piece contains the opinions of Trading Central and does not constitute personalized investment advice or form part of any invitation or inducement to buy or sell any security. The author has been prohibited by Trading Central from purchasing or otherwise directly or indirectly acquiring any direct or indirect beneficial ownership of any instruments or markets for which Trading Central or its affiliates issues recommendations. To read more, visit bit.ly/1MehCU9.] (analysts-europe@tradingcentral.com)\par \par \uc2 0742 GMT - \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  's global bond team has currently a small tactical long position in Italian government debt on valuation grounds and is overweight the front end of the German Bund curve, Marilyn Watson, head of global fundamental fixed income strategy, says. The asset manager reckons the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will maintain a cautious and gradual approach to removing its very loose monetary policy stance, Ms. Watson says. While Italian government bond yields trade at elevated levels amid the budget dispute between Italy's government and the \uc2 European Commission\uc2  , there are views elsewhere too that the valuations are or may become tactically attractive once rating risks are off the table. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0729 GMT - The dollar had a backseat position this week thanks to the Italian budget proposal and \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting, but this may change today. The first estimate of U.S. third-quarter gross domestic product is due for release and market participants will watch it closely to see whether economic growth continues to be strong. "A stronger print may help to support flagging risk appetite," \uc2 RBC\uc2  says. It says its forecasts of a 4% increase are "well ahead of consensus." A WSJ poll of economists forecasts a rise of 3.4% compared with a 4.2% rise in the previous quarter, however. The EUR/USD is flat at 1.1380. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0728 GMT - Sterling trades flat on Friday, both against the dollar and the euro. The pound "remains in its usual state of flummox as the Brexit impasse continues, with politics at home the biggest stumbling block," ING says. GBP/USD is at 1.2821 and EUR/GBP is at 0.8879. But ING says that at this level, GBP/USD "presents a good opportunity to buy" sterling again because 1.30 is its neutral level for now "if one believes that Brexit will in fact be alright on the night." The Dutch bank says GBP/USD will continue trading below 1.30 as long as the Brexit impasse isn't resolved. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0710 GMT - The euro is flat on Friday and an S&P rating decision on Italian debt is unlikely greatly to affect the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , says \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  . The agency announces its rating for Italy after \uc2 Moody's\uc2  decision last week. "The dialogue between the Italian government and the \uc2 European Commission\uc2  , which was also highlighted by \uc2 ECB\uc2  President \uc2 Mario Draghi\uc2  in yesterday's press conference, will be more important," \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  says. An improvement in the political picture, as well as an improvement in economic sentiment, will probably be needed to spark a recovery in the euro, the bank says. EUR/USD at 1.1370 and EUR/GBP at 0.8876. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 26, 2018 05:33 ET (09:33 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020181026eeaq000ys\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
