\par\par \b \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2  Steps Up to Slow Yuan Devaluation -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,218 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 2018\par 17:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 1109 ET - There are signs that the \uc2 People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, says \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  . "We're seeing PBC getting more active in slowing the depreciation," \uc2 RBC\uc2  CM says. September balance sheet data show that PBC sold $17.4 billion of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the largest direct \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since early 2017. The Chinese yuan fell to a record low on Thursday, sending USD/CNY up to 6.9526. The PBC bought a record of $66.3 billion on Wednesday, exceeding the previous high of $56.79 billion, when \b \highlight22\uc2 China intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively immediately after the August 2015 devaluation, \uc2 RBC\uc2  CM says. USD/CNY is last flat at 6.9490. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1106 ET - A group of state bank regulators reinitiated a lawsuit against \uc2 the Office of the Comptroller of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  over its plan to charter fintech companies as limited-purpose banks. The Conference of State Bank Supervisors filed a complaint in federal court in the District of Columbia, arguing the OCC does not have the authority to provide such charters, which would preempt certain state laws including interest rate limits. The group's original lawsuit was dismissed in April because the OCC had not taken any concrete steps to implement the charter yet. New York's banking regulator also reinitiated a lawsuit opposing the plan in September, after an earlier challenge was dismissed over similar reasons. The OCC announced in July that it would begin accepting fintech charter applications under its new Trump-appointed head \uc2 Joseph Otting\uc2  . (lalita.clozel@wsj.com; @laliczl)\par \par \uc2 1059 ET - If EUR/NOK were to fall below 9.40 in coming weeks, \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  would recommend buying it, mainly because of the Norwegian krone's "vulnerability to external events towards year-end." But for 2019, "we still pencil in a lower EUR/NOK," says \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  . It remains short EUR/NOK, but it is "increasingly contemplating taking profit" if it falls. EUR/NOK is last down 0.4% at 9.4776 after the \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2  earlier left interest rates unchanged and signalled it would raise the interest rate in the first quarter next year. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1029 ET - The bar for the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shift away from the current stance is "relatively high," says \uc2 Anna Stupnytska\uc2 , global economist at \uc2 Fidelity International\uc2 , adding that this is in particular true for the asset purchase program. "If economic weakness becomes more broad-based over the next few months, they are more likely to tweak their forward guidance on interest rates, rather than extend QE beyond December 2018," she adds. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0954 ET - The \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2  "a bit surprisingly" said that developments in both the labor and housing markets were "broadly as expected" in its statement earlier Thursday, says \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  , which had anticipated "some negative remarks" on both. The \uc2 Norwegian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also made no comment about the unusually dry summer influencing higher core inflation, though \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  says it had expected this. \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2  kept rates at 0.75%, and said another rate rise was likely in 1Q. \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  expects a rate rise in March. (jessica.fleetham@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0940 ET - Treasurys are searching for direction as stocks take center stage again following their sharp declines Wednesday. After peaking earlier this month, yields have often been pushed around by stocks, with investors seeking safety in Treasurys when stocks swoon. The 10-year yield was recently 3.120% vs. 3.122% Wednesday and 3.198% at the end of last week. (sam.goldfarb@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0938 ET - The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is currently on autopilot and "the recent Italian turbulence hasn't altered this," says Barry McAndrew, fixed income senior portfolio manager for EMEA at \uc2 State Street Global Advisors\uc2 . He adds that the \uc2 ECB\uc2  continues to see risks as broadly balanced. Despite below-target inflation expectations, the \uc2 ECB\uc2  sees "small pockets of wage pressure," says McAndrew, adding that this gives the \uc2 ECB\uc2  some confidence that policy should be less accommodative. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0925 ET - The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  's Governing Council still anticipates that net asset purchases will end at the end of the year, but, "interestingly, decided not to drop the conditionality," says \uc2 Swedbank\uc2 . As before, the decision will be subject to data confirming the medium-term outlook, says \uc2 Swedbank\uc2 's analyst Nerijus Maciulis. He adds that is could be perceived as a dovish statement. \uc2 Swedbank\uc2  maintains its forecasts that the \uc2 ECB\uc2  will raise its deposit rate by 15 basis points in September 2019 and raise both deposit and main refinancing rates by 25 basis points in December 2019. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0920 ET - The euro edges up slightly during the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  press conference, taking EUR/USD up 0.3% to 1.1430. President \uc2 Mario Draghi\uc2  reiterated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy forecasts and said the quantitative easing program would end by the end of this year. Before the conference some analysts had highlighted risks that Mr. Draghi could signal hesitation about ending the program, given that Italy is aiming for a fiscal deficit that is higher than the \uc2 European Commission\uc2  is comfortable with. The euro remains below 1.15 against the dollar, however, a level it breached recently on a mix of Italian budget uncertainties and weaker-than-expected economic data. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0916 ET - Italian government bond yields are trading significantly lower, reinforcing a trend that started earlier in the day, indicating a better risk appetite, as \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President \uc2 Mario Draghi\uc2  is speaking. The 10-year Italian BTP yield is trading 11 basis points lower at 3.51%, according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2  . There "wasn't much discussion" on Italy's Budget, Mr. Draghi says. Eurozone core government bond yields trade higher with the 10-year Bund yield up 2.5 basis points at 0.41%. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0907 ET - B&M's fully debt-funded acquisition of Babou entails material execution risk and is negative for its credit, says Victor Garcia, \uc2 Moody's Investors Service\uc2  lead analyst for B&M. "The acquisition multiple of 3.7x enterprise value/EBITDA seems very low for the industry standards, implying that Babou may have problems with its business model and/or operating performance," he says. The European retailer's Ba3 rating, however, remains "strongly positioned and benefits from ample headroom in the current rating category."(lorena.ruibal@wsj.com; @lorena_rbal)\par \par \uc2 0855 ET - As long as "the Norwegian economy stays on track, and the rest of the world doesn't fall off a cliff, we expect the \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2  will follow through on the first-quarter hike," says ING. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its interest rate unchanged on Thursday at 0.75%, but said it will raise the rate for the second time in 1Q19. ING reckons this will be in March, "given the NB's preference to move policy at meetings where they have new forecasts and a press conference." EUR/NOK is last down 0.2% at 9.4954.(olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 25, 2018 11:09 ET (15:09 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020181025eeap002l1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
