\par\par \b \uc2 BREAKINGVIEWS-U.S. Treasury hasn\u8217\'20\'19t yet been Trumped\b0\par\par\uc2 646 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2018\par 01:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (The author is a Reuters Breakingviews columnist. The opinions expressed are her own.)\par \par \uc2 By Gina Chon\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON, Oct 17 (Reuters Breakingviews) - China again escaped being named a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator by the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  on Wednesday. That's despite pressure from President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Although the trade-related penalties that could follow from the label are already happening through other means, it\u8217\'20\'19s a rational decision offering some comfort to investors.\par \par \uc2 Trump has repeatedly called on U.S. Treasury Secretary \uc2 Steven Mnuchin\uc2  to slap the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator designation onto China. The yuan has weakened relative to the U.S. dollar by about 6 percent this year, and Mnuchin said earlier this month that China\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves would be a key part of trade talks.\par \par \uc2 But he also told Reuters that the twice-yearly \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  report is not a political document. By law, a major U.S. trading partner has to meet three criteria to be labeled a manipulator, including one-sided \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. Treasury said \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s exchange-rate practices continue to lack transparency, but that direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year has been limited.\par \par \uc2 As it happens, being labeled a manipulator would have limited consequences for China. Trade actions after a year of talks are the most significant potential reprisal and U.S. tariffs have already moved well beyond that. Since the last Treasury \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  report in April, the United States has imposed duties on about $250 billion in Chinese goods, about half of total imports.\par \par \uc2 Still, at least it's a decision by the book. The Treasury has also been consistent in its reviews of foreign deals. Under President Barack Obama's administration, the \uc2 Committee on Foreign Investment in the United States\uc2  took a fairly tough line on Chinese deals given a raft of intellectual property theft cases. The panel under Mnuchin has followed that playbook, with Congress recently granting it expanded powers.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  under Chairman \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  has also maintained its autonomy. The president has attacked the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent interviews for raising interest rates too much. Fed policymakers appear unmoved and likely to raise rates again in December, according to minutes of last month\u8217\'20\'19s meeting released on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Trump told Fox News this week that the Fed was his biggest threat, yet \u8220\'20\'1Cit\u8217\'20\'19s independent so I don\u8217\'20\'19t speak to them.\u8221\'20\'1D Mnuchin isn't insulated in the same way, but the \uc2 U.S. Treasury Department\uc2  hasn\u8217\'20\'19t yet been Trumped.\par \par \uc2 On \uc2 Twitter{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GinaChon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://twitter.com/GinaChon}}}\par \par \uc2 CONTEXT NEWS\par \par \uc2 - The \uc2 U.S. Treasury Department\uc2  did not label any country, including China, as a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator in its latest twice-yearly report on the matter, released on Oct. 17. \u8220\'20\'1COf particular concern are China\u8217\'20\'19s lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  transparency and the recent weakness in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Treasury Secretary \uc2 Steven Mnuchin\uc2  said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CThese pose major challenges to achieving fairer and more balanced trade, and we will continue to monitor and review China\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  practices, including through ongoing discussions with the \uc2 People\u8217\'20\'19s Bank of China\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 - No new countries were added to the monitoring list since the April report. The six countries being watched are China, Germany, India, Japan, South Korea, and Switzerland. A country has to meet three conditions to be labeled a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator, which can spark trade actions. The factors are a bilateral trade surplus of at least $20 billion, a current-account surplus that is at least 3 percent of GDP and persistent, one-sided \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in net purchases of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that total at least 2 percent of an economy\u8217\'20\'19s GDP over a 12-month period.\par \par \uc2 - For previous columns by the author, Reuters customers can click on\par \par \uc2 - SIGN UP FOR BREAKINGVIEWS EMAIL ALERTS {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://bit.ly/BVsubscribe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://bit.ly/BVsubscribe}}}\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Richard Beales and Martin Langfield) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-10-18T00:49:53.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020181017eeah03zr1\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li5